        "custom_liquid_NazKBY": {
          "type": "custom-liquid",
          "name": "Advanced Shipping Box",
          "settings": {
            "custom_liquid": "{%- comment -%}\n============================================================\n  ESG SHIPPING BAR — UNIVERSAL\n  Paste target: Custom Liquid block on the product template\n  (or snippets/esg-shipping-bar.liquid + a render tag)\n\n  Replaces three separate blocks:\n    esg-ship        (in stock countdown / out of stock window)\n    esg-fship       (free next day air / 2-day air, tag driven)\n    esg-avail       (backorder + built-to-order lead time)\n\n  ONE BAR. FOUR STATES. NEVER MORE THAN ONE VISIBLE.\n\n  ---- PRECEDENCE (top wins) --------------------------------\n    0  SHIPS DIRECT FROM <SUPPLIER>\n                    outranks even the air-freight promise. ESG\n                    cannot commit another company's warehouse\n                    to a next-day handoff, and the copy says\n                    plainly that ordering through Elite Sim\n                    Golf does not cancel or shorten the\n                    supplier's backorder and lead times.\n                    Inside this state the item's OWN\n                    backorder:/leadtime: tags still drive the\n                    detail line and the badge, so per-item\n                    windows keep working exactly as before;\n                    with neither tag it falls back to\n                    dropship_default_lead.\n    1  FREE NEXT DAY AIR / FREE 2-DAY AIR\n                    a freeshipping tag OUTRANKS everything. The\n                    air-freight promise is a commercial\n                    commitment on a ready-to-ship item, so it\n                    is never diluted by a lead time, a build\n                    window or a backorder notice. If a product\n                    should not carry that promise, remove the\n                    tag - do not rely on stock to suppress it.\n                    Set svc_respects_stock = true to let an\n                    out-of-stock variant fall through to 4.\n    2  BACKORDER    stock shortfall is the binding constraint\n    4  IN STOCK     countdown to cutoff, or next business day.\n                    Stock outranks a leadtime: tag - a built-\n                    to-order item with units on hand ships\n                    from those units; the build window only\n                    fires once inventory hits zero.\n    5  BUILT TO ORDER (leadtime)   production window, shown\n                    only when the selected variant has no\n                    inventory. Unknown inventory still trips\n                    it as a safe default.\n    6  AVAILABLE TO ORDER   estimated 1-3 business day window\n\n  States 1 and 4 share one element; the freeshipping tag swaps\n  the headline, icon and copy.\n\n  This precedence is why the old shipmin:2 workaround is gone.\n  A next-day-air promise can no longer print next to a\n  backorder notice or a build window because they are the same\n  element and only one state is ever visible.\n\n  ---- TAGS (case insensitive, - _ and : tolerated) ---------\n    freeshipping:nda      Free Next Day Air  / UPS Next Day Air\n    freeshipping:2day     Free 2-Day Air     / UPS 2nd Day Air\n                          nda wins if both are present\n\n    backorder             always shows\n    backorder:<eta>       always shows, names an expected date\n    backorder:auto        shows only when the SELECTED variant\n                          is at or below 0 on hand\n    bo / bo:<eta>         alias\n                          backorder:auto + backorder:<eta> can\n                          be combined: one sets the mode, the\n                          other supplies the date\n\n    leadtime:<duration>   build-to-order production window\n    lead:<duration>       alias\n    lead-time:<duration>  alias (hyphen in the head is ignored)\n\n    shipsfrom:carls-place   ships direct from Carl's Place\n    carls-place             bare alias, same result\n    ships-from:<alias>      any other supplier; hyphens become\n    shipfrom:<alias>        spaces and each word is capitalized\n    supplier:<Display Name> exact casing and punctuation, e.g.\n                            supplier:Carl's Place - use this for\n                            any name capitalize would mangle\n\n    shipname:<value>      display name override; the Shopify\n                          title stays SEO-loaded while the bar\n                          reads \"Garmin Approach R50\".\n                          Split on the FIRST colon only, so\n                          colons in the name survive.\n\n  ---- ETA / DURATION VALUES --------------------------------\n    Dates      backorder:2026-10-15        -> October 15, 2026\n               (YYYY-MM-DD only, detected by a 4-digit year)\n    Ranges     leadtime:4-6-weeks          -> 4-6 weeks\n    Single     leadtime:6-weeks            -> 6 weeks\n    Multi-word leadtime:10-14-business-days -> 10-14 business days\n    Trailing words become the unit, so days, weeks, months and\n    business days all work with no code change. An unparseable\n    value degrades to raw text with hyphens turned into spaces.\n    A malformed date (2026-13-01) drops the eta rather than\n    falling through to the duration parser.\n\n  ---- VARIANT AWARE ---------------------------------------\n    Inventory is read per variant, never summed. A 24-variant\n    impact screen can have one size in stock and another\n    backordered; summing hides that, and oversold negative\n    quantities cancel out positive ones. Variants with\n    inventory tracking off are always treated as in stock.\n    The visible state re-resolves when the shopper changes\n    variant — including theme pickers that fire no native\n    change event, which is why the id is also polled.\n\n  ---- CONFIG ----------------------------------------------\n    cutoff_hour and cutoff_text must be changed together.\n    Holidays are NOT handled — only Sat/Sun are skipped, so a\n    UPS holiday on a weekday still reads as a ship day.\n    Partial shipments and split orders are not modelled. The\n    copy describes a SHIP window only, never a delivery date.\n\n  All tag-derived text is passed through | escape; Shopify\n  does not auto-escape and both the display name and the eta\n  come from merchant tags. JS copy is built as DOM text nodes\n  so a product name can never be parsed as markup.\n\n  Styling matches the accessories, projector fitment and\n  related blocks: navy #0A1A3A, no gradients, no radius, 1px\n  #E6E9F0 border with a 3px navy top accent, Barlow Condensed\n  headings, Inter body.\n============================================================\n{%- endcomment -%}\n\n{%- liquid\n  assign cutoff_hour = 14\n  assign cutoff_text = '2:00 PM ET'\n  assign lead_min = 1\n  assign lead_max = 3\n\n  # Direct-ship / supplier default window, used only when a supplier product\n  # carries no backorder: or leadtime: tag of its own. Per-item leadtime tags\n  # always override this.\n  assign dropship_default_lead = '3-5 business days'\n\n  # freeshipping tags outrank backorder and lead time. Flip this to true only\n  # if you want an out-of-stock variant on a freeshipping product to drop to\n  # the estimated ship window instead of holding the air-freight promise.\n  assign svc_respects_stock = false\n\n  assign months = 'January,February,March,April,May,June,July,August,September,October,November,December' | split: ','\n\n  # ---- read tags -------------------------------------------\n  assign svc_key = ''\n  assign name_tag = ''\n  assign bo_seen = false\n  assign bo_auto = false\n  assign bo_val = ''\n  assign lead_seen = false\n  assign lead_val = ''\n  assign sup_key = ''\n  assign sup_raw = ''\n  assign sup_name = ''\n\n  for tag in product.tags\n    assign t = tag | strip | downcase | replace: '_', ':'\n    assign parts = t | split: ':'\n    # the head may be written lead-time or lead_time; the value must keep\n    # its hyphens because ranges and dates are hyphen separated\n    assign head = parts[0] | default: '' | replace: '-', ''\n    assign val = parts[1] | default: ''\n\n    # free shipping trigger: hyphens are collapsed to colons here so\n    # freeshipping-nda and freeshipping:next-day both land\n    assign tf = t | replace: '-', ':'\n    if tf == 'freeshipping:nda' or tf == 'freeshipping:next:day' or tf == 'freeshipping:nextday'\n      assign svc_key = 'nda'\n    endif\n    if tf == 'freeshipping:2day' or tf == 'freeshipping:2:day' or tf == 'freeshipping:two:day'\n      if svc_key == ''\n        assign svc_key = '2day'\n      endif\n    endif\n\n    if head == 'backorder' or head == 'bo'\n      assign bo_seen = true\n      if val == 'auto'\n        assign bo_auto = true\n      elsif val != ''\n        assign bo_val = val\n      endif\n    endif\n\n    if head == 'leadtime' or head == 'lead'\n      if val != ''\n        assign lead_seen = true\n        assign lead_val = val\n      endif\n    endif\n\n    # ---- direct-ship supplier -----------------------------\n    # shipsfrom:<alias>, ships-from:<alias>, shipfrom:<alias>, or the bare\n    # alias tag on its own. Hyphens in the alias are collapsed so carls-place,\n    # carlsplace and carls all land on the same supplier.\n    if head == 'shipsfrom' or head == 'shipfrom'\n      assign sup_key = val | replace: '-', ''\n      assign sup_raw = val\n    endif\n    if head == 'carlsplace' or head == 'carls'\n      assign sup_key = 'carlsplace'\n      assign sup_raw = 'carls-place'\n    endif\n\n    # shipname: keeps its original casing, so test the raw tag.\n    # size comes off the UNSTRIPPED first segment so the slice index\n    # stays aligned with the raw string, e.g. 'shipname :Foo'\n    assign raw = tag | strip\n    assign probe = raw | downcase\n    if probe contains 'shipname:'\n      assign seg0 = raw | split: ':' | first\n      assign h2 = seg0 | strip | downcase\n      if h2 == 'shipname'\n        assign cut = seg0 | size | plus: 1\n        assign name_tag = raw | slice: cut, 255 | strip\n      endif\n    endif\n\n    # supplier:<Display Name> sets an arbitrary supplier with its casing and\n    # punctuation intact, e.g. supplier:Carl's Place. Same first-colon split\n    # as shipname, so a colon inside the name survives.\n    if probe contains 'supplier:'\n      assign seg1 = raw | split: ':' | first\n      assign h3 = seg1 | strip | downcase\n      if h3 == 'supplier'\n        assign cut2 = seg1 | size | plus: 1\n        assign sup_name = raw | slice: cut2, 255 | strip\n      endif\n    endif\n  endfor\n\n  # ---- supplier display name -------------------------------\n  # Known aliases first, then any supplier: override, then a tidied alias.\n  if sup_name == ''\n    if sup_key == 'carlsplace'\n      assign sup_name = \"Carl's Place\"\n    elsif sup_raw != ''\n      # capitalize only touches the first character, so words are title-cased\n      # one at a time. Suppliers with punctuation should use supplier:<Name>.\n      assign words = sup_raw | replace: '-', ' ' | split: ' '\n      assign built = ''\n      for w in words\n        assign cw = w | capitalize\n        assign built = built | append: ' ' | append: cw\n      endfor\n      assign sup_name = built | strip\n    endif\n  endif\n  assign is_sup = false\n  if sup_name != ''\n    assign is_sup = true\n  endif\n\n  # ---- eta / duration values ------------------------------\n  # Parsed for BOTH slots, not just the winner. backorder:auto plus a\n  # leadtime tag can flip between states on the client, so the lead-time\n  # badge must never inherit the backorder date.\n  assign bo_text = ''\n  assign bo_short = ''\n  assign lead_text = ''\n  assign lead_short = ''\n\n  for slot in (1..2)\n    if slot == 1\n      assign pval = bo_val\n    else\n      assign pval = lead_val\n    endif\n\n  assign val_kind = ''\n  assign val_text = ''\n  assign val_short = ''\n  assign segs = pval | split: '-'\n  assign nsegs = segs | size\n  assign s0 = segs[0] | default: ''\n  assign s0len = s0 | size\n\n  assign is_date = false\n  if nsegs == 3 and s0len == 4\n    assign is_date = true\n  endif\n\n  if is_date\n    assign mo = segs[1] | plus: 0\n    assign dy = segs[2] | plus: 0\n    assign mi = mo | minus: 1\n    assign mname = months[mi] | default: ''\n    if mname != '' and mo > 0 and mo < 13 and dy > 0 and dy < 32\n      assign val_kind = 'date'\n      assign val_text = mname | append: ' ' | append: dy | append: ', ' | append: segs[0]\n      assign val_short = mname | slice: 0, 3 | append: ' ' | append: dy\n    else\n      # A malformed date must not fall through to the duration parser, which\n      # would happily read 2026-13-01 as a range. Drop the eta instead: the\n      # bar still renders, just without a date it cannot trust.\n      assign val_kind = 'bad'\n      assign val_text = ''\n    endif\n  endif\n\n  if val_kind == '' and pval != ''\n    # leading numeric segments are the amount, everything after is the unit.\n    # Amounts are held in two named vars rather than a delimited string:\n    # Shopify drops a trailing empty on split, python-liquid keeps it, so a\n    # '6,' accumulator counts as 1 in production and 2 in test.\n    assign n1 = ''\n    assign n2 = ''\n    assign unit_parts = ''\n    for seg in segs\n      assign sn = seg | plus: 0\n      assign back = sn | append: ''\n      if back == seg and unit_parts == ''\n        if n1 == ''\n          assign n1 = seg\n        elsif n2 == ''\n          assign n2 = seg\n        endif\n      else\n        if seg != ''\n          assign unit_parts = unit_parts | append: seg | append: ' '\n        endif\n      endif\n    endfor\n    assign unit = unit_parts | strip\n    if n1 != '' and unit != ''\n      assign val_kind = 'duration'\n      if n2 == ''\n        assign val_text = n1 | append: ' ' | append: unit\n      else\n        assign val_text = n1 | append: '–' | append: n2 | append: ' ' | append: unit\n      endif\n      assign val_short = val_text\n    else\n      # unparseable: show it rather than dropping it\n      assign val_kind = 'raw'\n      assign val_text = pval | replace: '-', ' '\n      assign val_short = val_text\n    endif\n  endif\n\n    if slot == 1\n      assign bo_text = val_text\n      assign bo_short = val_short\n    else\n      assign lead_text = val_text\n      assign lead_short = val_short\n    endif\n  endfor\n\n  # ---- per-variant inventory map ---------------------------\n  # untracked_qty is the sentinel written for variants that have Shopify's\n  # \"Track quantity\" turned off. A tagged untracked product (freeshipping,\n  # leadtime, supplier, backorder) uses the in-stock sentinel so those tags\n  # keep working. An UNtagged untracked product is treated as unknown stock\n  # instead, which routes it to the Estimated Ship Date (1-3 day) window --\n  # any_tag is the flag that decides between the two.\n  assign any_tag = false\n  if svc_key != '' or bo_seen or lead_seen or is_sup\n    assign any_tag = true\n  endif\n\n  assign untracked_qty = 999999\n  if any_tag == false\n    # 'unknown' sentinel: the client-side pick() treats a non-numeric qty as\n    # 'no stock info', so an untracked-and-untagged product lands on 'out'\n    # instead of 'in'. The map string still parses cleanly.\n    assign untracked_qty = 'unknown'\n  endif\n\n  assign cur = product.selected_or_first_available_variant\n  assign sel_id = cur.id | default: ''\n  assign inv_map = ''\n  assign sel_qty = 0\n  assign have_sel = false\n\n  for v in product.variants\n    assign im = v.inventory_management | default: ''\n    if im == ''\n      assign q = untracked_qty\n    else\n      assign q = v.inventory_quantity | plus: 0\n    endif\n    assign inv_map = inv_map | append: v.id | append: ':' | append: q | append: ','\n    assign vid = v.id | append: ''\n    assign sid = sel_id | append: ''\n    if vid == sid\n      assign sel_qty = q\n      assign have_sel = true\n    endif\n  endfor\n\n  unless have_sel\n    assign im = cur.inventory_management | default: ''\n    if im == ''\n      assign sel_qty = untracked_qty\n    else\n      assign sel_qty = cur.inventory_quantity | plus: 0\n    endif\n  endunless\n\n  # sel_qty is used in server-side comparisons below (sel_qty > 0, etc). The\n  # 'unknown' string coerces to 0 via | plus: 0, so those comparisons behave\n  # the same as \"no stock known\" (falls to the estimated ship window).\n  assign sel_qty_num = sel_qty | plus: 0\n\n  # ---- direct-ship sub-state -------------------------------\n  # Inside the supplier state the detail line still follows the item's own\n  # tags: a backorder wins, then stock (if any) beats the build window, then\n  # a per-item leadtime, then the house default. Stock overrides leadtime so\n  # a Carl's Place item with units on hand ships from those units instead of\n  # promising a production window the customer would not actually wait on.\n  assign sup_detail = 'default'\n  if bo_seen and bo_auto == false\n    assign sup_detail = 'bo'\n  elsif bo_seen and bo_auto and sel_qty_num <= 0\n    assign sup_detail = 'bo'\n  elsif sel_qty_num > 0\n    assign sup_detail = 'default'\n  elsif lead_seen\n    assign sup_detail = 'lead'\n  endif\n\n  assign def_text = dropship_default_lead | replace: '-', '–'\n\n  # ---- resolve the initial state (JS re-resolves on change) -\n  # A supplier tag outranks even the air-freight promise: ESG cannot commit\n  # another company's warehouse to a next-day handoff. A freeshipping tag\n  # OUTRANKS everything else. An air-freight promise is a\n  # commercial commitment on a stocked, ready-to-ship item, so it must never\n  # be paired with a build window, a backorder notice, or an estimated\n  # multi-day window. Set svc_respects_stock = true below if you instead want\n  # out-of-stock variants to fall through to the estimated ship window.\n  assign state = 'out'\n  if is_sup\n    assign state = 'sup'\n  elsif svc_key != '' and svc_respects_stock == false\n    assign state = 'in'\n  elsif svc_key != '' and sel_qty_num > 0\n    assign state = 'in'\n  elsif bo_seen and bo_auto == false\n    assign state = 'bo'\n  elsif bo_seen and bo_auto and sel_qty_num <= 0\n    assign state = 'bo'\n  elsif sel_qty_num > 0\n    # Stock outranks a leadtime: tag. A built-to-order item with units on the\n    # shelf ships from those units; the production window is only relevant\n    # once stock runs out.\n    assign state = 'in'\n  elsif lead_seen\n    assign state = 'lead'\n  endif\n\n  assign bo_mode = ''\n  if bo_seen\n    if bo_auto\n      assign bo_mode = 'auto'\n    else\n      assign bo_mode = 'always'\n    endif\n  endif\n\n  # ---- service level copy ---------------------------------\n  assign svc_headline = 'In Stock'\n  assign svc_meta = 'Ready To Ship · 30-Day Returns*'\n  assign service = ''\n  if svc_key == 'nda'\n    assign svc_headline = 'Free Next Day Air'\n    assign svc_meta = 'Authorized Reseller · Free Returns'\n    assign service = 'UPS Next Day Air'\n  elsif svc_key == '2day'\n    assign svc_headline = 'Free 2-Day Air'\n    assign svc_meta = 'Authorized Reseller · Free Returns'\n    assign service = 'UPS 2nd Day Air'\n  endif\n\n  # ---- display name: tag override, then product title -----\n  assign disp = name_tag | default: ''\n  if disp == ''\n    assign disp = product.title\n  endif\n-%}\n\n<link rel=\"preconnect\" href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com\">\n<link rel=\"preconnect\" href=\"https://fonts.gstatic.com\" crossorigin>\n<link href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Barlow+Condensed:wght@600;700;800;900&family=Inter:wght@400;500;600;700&display=swap\" rel=\"stylesheet\">\n\n<div class=\"esg-bar\"\n     data-esg-bar\n     data-inv=\"{{ inv_map | escape }}\"\n     data-variant=\"{{ cur.id }}\"\n     data-cutoff-hour=\"{{ cutoff_hour }}\"\n     data-cutoff-text=\"{{ cutoff_text | escape }}\"\n     data-lead-min=\"{{ lead_min }}\"\n     data-lead-max=\"{{ lead_max }}\"\n     data-bo=\"{{ bo_mode }}\"\n     data-has-lead=\"{% if lead_seen %}1{% else %}0{% endif %}\"\n     data-name=\"{{ disp | escape }}\"\n     data-service=\"{{ service | escape }}\"\n     data-svc=\"{% if svc_key != '' %}1{% else %}0{% endif %}\"\n     data-svc-strict=\"{% if svc_respects_stock %}1{% else %}0{% endif %}\"\n     data-sup=\"{% if is_sup %}1{% else %}0{% endif %}\"\n     data-bo-short=\"{{ bo_short | escape }}\"\n     data-lead-short=\"{{ lead_short | escape }}\"\n     data-def-short=\"{{ def_text | escape }}\">\n\n  {%- comment -%} 0 · Direct from supplier (Carl's Place et al) {%- endcomment -%}\n  {%- if is_sup -%}\n  <div class=\"esg-bar__state esg-bar__state--sup\" data-state=\"sup\" {% unless state == 'sup' %}hidden{% endunless %}>\n    <span class=\"esg-bar__icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n      <svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">\n        <path d=\"M3 9.5 12 4l9 5.5\"></path>\n        <path d=\"M5 9.8V20h14V9.8\"></path>\n        <path d=\"M9.5 20v-5.5h5V20\"></path>\n      </svg>\n    </span>\n\n    <div class=\"esg-bar__body\">\n      <span class=\"esg-bar__ttlrow\">\n        <span class=\"esg-bar__title\">Ships Direct From {{ sup_name | escape }}</span>\n        <span class=\"esg-bar__meta\">Authorized Dealer · Factory Direct</span>\n      </span>\n\n      {%- comment -%} one detail line per case; JS re-picks on variant change {%- endcomment -%}\n      <span class=\"esg-bar__text\" data-sup-detail=\"bo\" {% unless sup_detail == 'bo' %}hidden{% endunless %}>\n        The <strong>{{ disp | escape }}</strong> ships direct from {{ sup_name | escape }} and is currently on backorder{% if bo_text != '' %}, expected <strong>{{ bo_text | escape }}</strong>{% endif %}. Ordering through Elite Sim Golf does not cancel or shorten {{ sup_name | escape }} backorder timelines.\n      </span>\n      <span class=\"esg-bar__text\" data-sup-detail=\"lead\" {% unless sup_detail == 'lead' %}hidden{% endunless %}>\n        The <strong>{{ disp | escape }}</strong> is built and shipped direct from {{ sup_name | escape }}. Production takes <strong>{{ lead_text | escape }}</strong> from the order date. Ordering through Elite Sim Golf does not shorten {{ sup_name | escape }} lead times.\n      </span>\n      <span class=\"esg-bar__text\" data-sup-detail=\"default\" {% unless sup_detail == 'default' %}hidden{% endunless %}>\n        The <strong>{{ disp | escape }}</strong> ships direct from {{ sup_name | escape }}, typically in <strong>{{ def_text | escape }}</strong>. Ordering through Elite Sim Golf does not change {{ sup_name | escape }} production or backorder timelines.\n      </span>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"esg-bar__aside\">\n      <span class=\"esg-bar__lbl\" data-sup-lbl>{% if sup_detail == 'bo' %}Expected{% elsif sup_detail == 'lead' %}Build Time{% else %}Ships In{% endif %}</span>\n      <span class=\"esg-bar__badge\" data-sup-badge>{% if sup_detail == 'bo' %}{{ bo_short | default: 'BACKORDER' | escape }}{% elsif sup_detail == 'lead' %}{{ lead_short | escape }}{% else %}{{ def_text | escape }}{% endif %}</span>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  {%- endif -%}\n\n  {%- comment -%} 1 · Backorder {%- endcomment -%}\n  <div class=\"esg-bar__state esg-bar__state--bo\" data-state=\"bo\" {% unless state == 'bo' %}hidden{% endunless %}>\n    <span class=\"esg-bar__icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n      <svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">\n        <path d=\"M21 8v11a1 1 0 0 1-1 1H4a1 1 0 0 1-1-1V8\"></path>\n        <rect x=\"2\" y=\"4\" width=\"20\" height=\"4\"></rect>\n        <polyline points=\"12 17 12 11\"></polyline>\n        <polyline points=\"9 14 12 11 15 14\"></polyline>\n      </svg>\n    </span>\n    <div class=\"esg-bar__body\">\n      <span class=\"esg-bar__ttlrow\">\n        <span class=\"esg-bar__title\">On Backorder</span>\n        <span class=\"esg-bar__meta\">Ships When Stock Arrives · 30-Day Returns</span>\n      </span>\n      <span class=\"esg-bar__text\">The <strong>{{ disp | escape }}</strong> is on backorder. Orders placed now reserve a unit from the next inbound shipment{% if bo_text != '' %}, expected <strong>{{ bo_text | escape }}</strong>{% endif %}.</span>\n    </div>\n    {%- if bo_text != '' -%}\n    <div class=\"esg-bar__aside\">\n      <span class=\"esg-bar__lbl\">Expected</span>\n      <span class=\"esg-bar__badge\">{{ bo_short | escape }}</span>\n    </div>\n    {%- endif -%}\n  </div>\n\n  {%- comment -%} 2 · Built to order {%- endcomment -%}\n  <div class=\"esg-bar__state esg-bar__state--lead\" data-state=\"lead\" {% unless state == 'lead' %}hidden{% endunless %}>\n    <span class=\"esg-bar__icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n      <svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">\n        <rect x=\"3\" y=\"5\" width=\"18\" height=\"16\"></rect>\n        <line x1=\"3\" y1=\"10\" x2=\"21\" y2=\"10\"></line>\n        <line x1=\"8\" y1=\"3\" x2=\"8\" y2=\"7\"></line>\n        <line x1=\"16\" y1=\"3\" x2=\"16\" y2=\"7\"></line>\n        <polyline points=\"9 15 11 17 15 13\"></polyline>\n      </svg>\n    </span>\n    <div class=\"esg-bar__body\">\n      <span class=\"esg-bar__ttlrow\">\n        <span class=\"esg-bar__title\">Built To Order</span>\n        <span class=\"esg-bar__meta\">Ships After Production · 30-Day Returns</span>\n      </span>\n      <span class=\"esg-bar__text\">The <strong>{{ disp | escape }}</strong> is built to order. Production takes <strong>{{ lead_text | escape }}</strong> from the order date, and the order ships as soon as the build is complete.</span>\n    </div>\n    {%- if lead_text != '' -%}\n    <div class=\"esg-bar__aside\">\n      <span class=\"esg-bar__lbl\">Build Time</span>\n      <span class=\"esg-bar__badge\">{{ lead_short | escape }}</span>\n    </div>\n    {%- endif -%}\n  </div>\n\n  {%- comment -%} 3 · In stock (free air upgrade when tagged) {%- endcomment -%}\n  <div class=\"esg-bar__state esg-bar__state--in\" data-state=\"in\" {% unless state == 'in' %}hidden{% endunless %}>\n    <span class=\"esg-bar__icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n      {%- if svc_key != '' -%}\n      <svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">\n        <rect x=\"1\" y=\"3\" width=\"15\" height=\"13\"></rect>\n        <polygon points=\"16 8 20 8 23 11 23 16 16 16 16 8\"></polygon>\n        <circle cx=\"5.5\" cy=\"18.5\" r=\"2.5\"></circle>\n        <circle cx=\"18.5\" cy=\"18.5\" r=\"2.5\"></circle>\n      </svg>\n      {%- else -%}\n      <svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.6\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><path d=\"M20 6 9 17l-5-5\"></path></svg>\n      {%- endif -%}\n    </span>\n    <div class=\"esg-bar__body\">\n      <span class=\"esg-bar__ttlrow\">\n        <span class=\"esg-bar__title\">{{ svc_headline }}</span>\n        <span class=\"esg-bar__meta\">{{ svc_meta }}</span>\n      </span>\n      <span class=\"esg-bar__text\" data-in-text>{% if service != '' %}Order your <strong>{{ disp | escape }}</strong> by <strong>{{ cutoff_text }}</strong> to ship today via <strong>{{ service }}</strong>.{% else %}Order by <strong>{{ cutoff_text }}</strong> to ship today.{% endif %}</span>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"esg-bar__aside\">\n      <span class=\"esg-bar__lbl\" data-in-label>Order Within</span>\n      <span class=\"esg-bar__badge\" data-in-badge>--:--:--</span>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  {%- comment -%} 4 · Available to order {%- endcomment -%}\n  <div class=\"esg-bar__state esg-bar__state--out\" data-state=\"out\" {% unless state == 'out' %}hidden{% endunless %}>\n    <span class=\"esg-bar__icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n      <svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.9\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"9\"></circle><path d=\"M12 7v5l3 2\"></path></svg>\n    </span>\n    <div class=\"esg-bar__body\">\n      <span class=\"esg-bar__ttlrow\">\n        <span class=\"esg-bar__title\">Estimated Ship Date</span>\n        <span class=\"esg-bar__meta\">Available To Order</span>\n      </span>\n      <span class=\"esg-bar__text\">Typically {{ lead_min }} to {{ lead_max }} business days after the order is placed{% if service != '' %}, then <strong>{{ service }}</strong>{% endif %}.</span>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"esg-bar__aside\">\n      <span class=\"esg-bar__lbl\">Ships</span>\n      <span class=\"esg-bar__badge\" data-out-badge>—</span>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div>\n\n<style>\n  .esg-bar{box-sizing:border-box;max-width:660px;margin:12px 0;background:#fff;border:1px solid #E6E9F0;border-top:3px solid #0A1A3A;color:#2a3756;font-family:'Inter',system-ui,-apple-system,sans-serif;line-height:1.4;--esg-bar-fg:#0A1A3A;--esg-bar-bd:#0A1A3A}\n  .esg-bar *{box-sizing:border-box}\n\n  /* Amber backorder variant: uncomment to switch. Nothing else changes.\n  .esg-bar__state--bo{--esg-bar-fg:#B45309;--esg-bar-bd:#B45309}\n  */\n\n  .esg-bar__state{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:12px;padding:10px 13px}\n  /* The UA sheet's [hidden]{display:none} loses to display:flex,\n     so the hidden state needs an explicit author rule. */\n  .esg-bar__state[hidden]{display:none}\n  /* display:block on the detail lines beats the UA [hidden] rule too */\n  .esg-bar__text[hidden]{display:none}\n\n  .esg-bar__icon{flex:0 0 32px;width:32px;height:32px;display:inline-flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;background:#fff;border:1px solid #E6E9F0;color:var(--esg-bar-fg)}\n  .esg-bar__icon svg{width:18px;height:18px;display:block}\n\n  .esg-bar__body{flex:1 1 220px;min-width:0}\n  .esg-bar__ttlrow{display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:8px;flex-wrap:wrap}\n  .esg-bar__title{font-family:'Barlow Condensed','Arial Narrow',sans-serif;font-size:17px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.02em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--esg-bar-fg);line-height:1.05}\n  .esg-bar__meta{font-family:'Barlow Condensed','Arial Narrow',sans-serif;font-size:11px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6B7390;line-height:1.1}\n  .esg-bar__text{display:block;font-size:12.5px;line-height:1.35;color:#2a3756;margin:3px 0 0}\n  .esg-bar__text strong{color:var(--esg-bar-fg);font-weight:700}\n\n  .esg-bar__aside{flex:0 0 auto;display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:flex-end;gap:4px;text-align:right}\n  .esg-bar__lbl{font-family:'Barlow Condensed','Arial Narrow',sans-serif;font-size:10.5px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6B7390;line-height:1;white-space:nowrap}\n  .esg-bar__badge{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;padding:6px 11px;background:var(--esg-bar-bd);border:1px solid var(--esg-bar-bd);border-radius:0;color:#fff;font-family:'Barlow Condensed','Arial Narrow',sans-serif;font-size:15px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.07em;line-height:1;text-transform:uppercase;white-space:nowrap;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}\n  .esg-bar__state--in .esg-bar__badge{font-size:17px;letter-spacing:.08em}\n\n  @media (max-width:749px){\n    .esg-bar__state{flex-wrap:wrap;padding:10px 12px}\n    .esg-bar__title{font-size:16px}\n    .esg-bar__text{font-size:12px}\n    .esg-bar__aside{flex:1 1 100%;flex-direction:row;align-items:center;justify-content:flex-start;gap:8px;padding-left:44px;text-align:left;margin-top:7px}\n    .esg-bar__badge,.esg-bar__state--in .esg-bar__badge{font-size:13px}\n  }\n</style>\n\n<script>\n(function () {\n  if (window.esgShipBar) { return; }\n  window.esgShipBar = true;\n\n  var TZ = 'America/New_York';\n  var DAYS = { Sun: 0, Mon: 1, Tue: 2, Wed: 3, Thu: 4, Fri: 5, Sat: 6 };\n\n  function pad(n) { return String(n).length < 2 ? '0' + n : String(n); }\n\n  function etFmt(d, opts) {\n    var o = { timeZone: TZ };\n    for (var k in opts) { if (Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(opts, k)) { o[k] = opts[k]; } }\n    return new Intl.DateTimeFormat('en-US', o).format(d);\n  }\n\n  function etDow(d) { return DAYS[etFmt(d, { weekday: 'short' })]; }\n\n  // Intl with hour12:false reports hour 24 at midnight in some engines.\n  function etSeconds(d) {\n    var p = {};\n    new Intl.DateTimeFormat('en-US', {\n      timeZone: TZ, hour: '2-digit', minute: '2-digit',\n      second: '2-digit', hour12: false\n    }).formatToParts(d).forEach(function (x) { p[x.type] = x.value; });\n    return (parseInt(p.hour, 10) % 24) * 3600 +\n           parseInt(p.minute, 10) * 60 +\n           parseInt(p.second, 10);\n  }\n\n  function isWeekend(d) { var w = etDow(d); return w === 0 || w === 6; }\n\n  // nth business day strictly after `from`, counting in ET\n  function businessDayAfter(from, n) {\n    var found = 0;\n    for (var i = 1; i <= 30; i++) {\n      var d = new Date(from.getTime() + i * 86400000);\n      if (!isWeekend(d)) {\n        found++;\n        if (found === n) { return d; }\n      }\n    }\n    return null;\n  }\n\n  function parseInv(raw) {\n    var map = {};\n    (raw || '').split(',').forEach(function (pair) {\n      if (!pair) { return; }\n      var bits = pair.split(':');\n      if (bits.length < 2) { return; }\n      var q = parseInt(bits[1], 10);\n      if (!isNaN(q)) { map[bits[0].trim()] = q; }\n    });\n    return map;\n  }\n\n  function selectedVariant(root) {\n    var q = new URLSearchParams(window.location.search).get('variant');\n    if (q) { return q.trim(); }\n    var form = root.closest('form[action*=\"/cart/add\"]') ||\n               document.querySelector('form[action*=\"/cart/add\"]');\n    var input = form && form.querySelector('input[name=\"id\"], select[name=\"id\"]');\n    if (input && input.value) { return String(input.value).trim(); }\n    return root.getAttribute('data-variant');\n  }\n\n  // Build sentences as DOM nodes so a product name is never parsed as markup.\n  function setCopy(el, parts) {\n    while (el.firstChild) { el.removeChild(el.firstChild); }\n    parts.forEach(function (part) {\n      if (typeof part === 'string') {\n        el.appendChild(document.createTextNode(part));\n        return;\n      }\n      var b = document.createElement('strong');\n      b.textContent = part.b;\n      el.appendChild(b);\n    });\n  }\n\n  function wire(root) {\n    if (root.getAttribute('data-esg-ready')) { return; }\n    root.setAttribute('data-esg-ready', '1');\n\n    var inv = parseInv(root.getAttribute('data-inv'));\n    var cutoffHour = parseInt(root.getAttribute('data-cutoff-hour'), 10);\n    if (isNaN(cutoffHour)) { cutoffHour = 14; }\n    var cutoffText = root.getAttribute('data-cutoff-text') || '2:00 PM ET';\n    var leadMin = parseInt(root.getAttribute('data-lead-min'), 10) || 1;\n    var leadMax = parseInt(root.getAttribute('data-lead-max'), 10) || 3;\n    var boMode = root.getAttribute('data-bo') || '';\n    var hasLead = root.getAttribute('data-has-lead') === '1';\n    var name = root.getAttribute('data-name') || 'this item';\n    var service = root.getAttribute('data-service') || '';\n    var hasSvc = root.getAttribute('data-svc') === '1';\n    var hasSup = root.getAttribute('data-sup') === '1';\n    var boShort = root.getAttribute('data-bo-short') || '';\n    var leadShort = root.getAttribute('data-lead-short') || '';\n    var defShort = root.getAttribute('data-def-short') || '';\n\n    function known(q) { return typeof q === 'number' && !isNaN(q); }\n    var svcStrict = root.getAttribute('data-svc-strict') === '1';\n\n    var states = {};\n    ['sup', 'bo', 'lead', 'in', 'out'].forEach(function (k) {\n      states[k] = root.querySelector('[data-state=\"' + k + '\"]');\n    });\n    var inLabel = root.querySelector('[data-in-label]');\n    var inBadge = root.querySelector('[data-in-badge]');\n    var inText = root.querySelector('[data-in-text]');\n    var outBadge = root.querySelector('[data-out-badge]');\n    var supLbl = root.querySelector('[data-sup-lbl]');\n    var supBadge = root.querySelector('[data-sup-badge]');\n    var supDetails = root.querySelectorAll('[data-sup-detail]');\n\n    function qtyFor() {\n      var vid = selectedVariant(root);\n      var q = inv[vid];\n      // unknown variant id: fall back to the Liquid-rendered default\n      if (typeof q !== 'number' || isNaN(q)) {\n        q = inv[root.getAttribute('data-variant')];\n      }\n      return q;\n    }\n\n    // Precedence: direct-ship supplier > free air > backorder > built to order\n    // > in stock > available to order. ESG cannot commit another company's\n    // warehouse to a next-day handoff, so the supplier state outranks the air\n    // promise; inside it the item's own backorder/leadtime tags still drive\n    // the detail line and badge. A freeshipping tag is a commercial commitment on a stocked,\n    // ready-to-ship item, so it never degrades into a lead time, a build\n    // window or a backorder notice. svcStrict lets an out-of-stock variant\n    // fall through instead.\n    function pick(qty) {\n      var ok = known(qty);\n      if (hasSup) { return 'sup'; }\n      if (hasSvc && (!svcStrict || (ok && qty > 0))) { return 'in'; }\n      if (boMode === 'always') { return 'bo'; }\n      if (boMode === 'auto' && ok && qty <= 0) { return 'bo'; }\n      // stock outranks a leadtime: tag - lead time only applies once we run\n      // out. If inventory is unknown the tag still wins as a safe default.\n      if (ok && qty > 0) { return 'in'; }\n      if (hasLead) { return 'lead'; }\n      return 'out';\n    }\n\n    function paint() {\n      var now = new Date();\n      var qty = qtyFor();\n      var active = pick(qty);\n\n      for (var k in states) {\n        if (states[k]) { states[k].hidden = (k !== active); }\n      }\n\n      if (active === 'sup') {\n        // The detail line follows the item's own tags, re-evaluated per\n        // variant so backorder:auto still tracks the selected size.\n        var detail = 'default';\n        if (boMode === 'always') { detail = 'bo'; }\n        else if (boMode === 'auto' && known(qty) && qty <= 0) { detail = 'bo'; }\n        else if (known(qty) && qty > 0) { detail = 'default'; }\n        else if (hasLead) { detail = 'lead'; }\n        for (var d = 0; d < supDetails.length; d++) {\n          supDetails[d].hidden = (supDetails[d].getAttribute('data-sup-detail') !== detail);\n        }\n        if (supLbl) {\n          supLbl.textContent = detail === 'bo' ? 'Expected'\n                             : detail === 'lead' ? 'Build Time' : 'Ships In';\n        }\n        if (supBadge) {\n          var t = detail === 'bo' ? boShort : detail === 'lead' ? leadShort : defShort;\n          supBadge.textContent = t || 'SEE DETAILS';\n        }\n      } else if (active === 'in') {\n        var secs = etSeconds(now);\n        var cutoff = cutoffHour * 3600;\n        var closed = isWeekend(now) || secs >= cutoff;\n\n        if (closed) {\n          var nb = businessDayAfter(now, 1);\n          if (inLabel) { inLabel.textContent = 'Ships'; }\n          if (inBadge) {\n            inBadge.textContent = nb\n              ? (etFmt(nb, { weekday: 'short' }) + ' · ' + etFmt(nb, { month: 'short', day: 'numeric' })).toUpperCase()\n              : '—';\n          }\n          if (inText) {\n            var when = nb\n              ? etFmt(nb, { weekday: 'long' }) + ', ' + etFmt(nb, { month: 'long', day: 'numeric' })\n              : 'the next business day';\n            if (service) {\n              setCopy(inText, ['The ', { b: name }, ' ships ', { b: when }, ' via ', { b: service }, '.']);\n            } else {\n              setCopy(inText, ['Ships ', { b: when }, '.']);\n            }\n          }\n        } else {\n          var r = cutoff - secs;\n          if (inLabel) { inLabel.textContent = 'Order Within'; }\n          if (inBadge) {\n            inBadge.textContent = pad(Math.floor(r / 3600)) + ':' +\n                                  pad(Math.floor((r % 3600) / 60)) + ':' +\n                                  pad(r % 60);\n          }\n          if (inText) {\n            if (service) {\n              setCopy(inText, ['Order your ', { b: name }, ' by ', { b: cutoffText },\n                               ' to ship today via ', { b: service }, '.']);\n            } else {\n              setCopy(inText, ['Order by ', { b: cutoffText }, ' to ship today.']);\n            }\n          }\n        }\n      } else if (active === 'out' && outBadge) {\n        var a = businessDayAfter(now, leadMin);\n        var b = businessDayAfter(now, leadMax);\n        if (a && b) {\n          var sameMonth = etFmt(a, { month: 'short' }) === etFmt(b, { month: 'short' });\n          outBadge.textContent = (etFmt(a, { month: 'short', day: 'numeric' }) + ' – ' +\n            (sameMonth ? etFmt(b, { day: 'numeric' })\n                       : etFmt(b, { month: 'short', day: 'numeric' }))).toUpperCase();\n        } else {\n          outBadge.textContent = '—';\n        }\n      }\n    }\n\n    paint();\n    setInterval(paint, 1000);\n\n    // Variant changes: native selects/radios inside the add-to-cart form,\n    // plus back/forward navigation that rewrites ?variant=. Themes whose\n    // pickers fire no native change event are covered by the 1s repaint.\n    var form = root.closest('form[action*=\"/cart/add\"]') || document;\n    form.addEventListener('change', paint);\n    document.addEventListener('change', paint);\n    window.addEventListener('popstate', paint);\n  }\n\n  function init() {\n    var nodes = document.querySelectorAll('[data-esg-bar]');\n    for (var i = 0; i < nodes.length; i++) { wire(nodes[i]); }\n  }\n\n  init();\n  if (document.readyState === 'loading') {\n    document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', init);\n  }\n  document.addEventListener('shopify:section:load', init);\n})();\n</script>"
          }
        },
        "custom_liquid_FB6kbp": {
          "type": "custom-liquid",
          "name": "ProTeeVX Swing Camera Promo",
          "settings": {
            "custom_liquid": "<!-- ============================================================\n     PROTEE VX — SWING CAMERA SET \"INCLUDED\" PROMO MODULE\n     ESG NAVY VERSION (no gold accents)\n\n     SELF-CONTAINED. Paste anywhere on any ProTee VX page\n     (standalone PDP, Premium 4K package pages, projector-combo\n     PDPs). No parent wrapper required.\n\n     LAYOUT: fixed 100x100 product thumbnail + copy, always a slim\n     horizontal strip (no stacking breakpoint) -- sized to sit\n     directly below the shipping/availability blocks without\n     dominating the page the way a full-width hero image would.\n\n     All classes namespaced .esg-vxpromo* so they cannot collide\n     with theme CSS or other ESG modules on the same page.\n\n     Recreates the reference \"Included\" strip (logo · checkmark ·\n     headline · copy) in the navy/light-gray system instead of\n     white/green. No countdown timer -- the \"Cameras Included\" badge\n     sits static on the left of the top strip. The right side of that\n     same strip now carries the ProTee \"Authorized Reseller\" logo\n     image instead of a text wordmark -- the \"ProTee VX Swing Camera\n     Set\" name is not printed anywhere in the top strip; it is\n     introduced once, in the body copy below, so the name only\n     appears a single time in the whole module.\n\n     TAG GATE: this block only renders on products tagged \"ProTee VX\"\n     (case-insensitive, exact tag match). Because Shopify's product\n     description field cannot run Liquid, the gate is done in JS: on\n     load it reads the current product's tags from the storefront's\n     public /products/<handle>.js endpoint (same endpoint the ESG\n     accessories block already uses) and only reveals the wrapper if\n     a matching tag is present. The wrapper ships with inline\n     style=\"display:none\" by default so nothing flashes on pages\n     where the tag check fails or the fetch errors.\n\n     TO CHANGE THE REQUIRED TAG, edit data-esg-vxpromo-tag on the\n     wrapper div. To disable the gate entirely (always show), remove\n     that attribute and the inline display:none.\n\n     If this same HTML/description field is only ever pasted onto\n     ProTee VX products anyway, the tag check is a safety net, not a\n     requirement -- but it means the identical snippet can safely be\n     synced into Popular-ProTee-VX-Accessories-style shared sections\n     or pasted onto a non-VX page by mistake without leaking the\n     promo there.\n\n     PASTE NOTE: paste in Shopify's HTML/code view (the < > button),\n     NOT the rich-text view -- rich text strips <style> blocks.\n\n     RESELLER BADGE: the ProTee \"Authorized Reseller\" logo is now\n     folded directly into the module's own top strip (right side,\n     opposite the \"Cameras Included\" pill) instead of sitting above it\n     as a separate block -- one card, one border, no duplicate tag\n     gate. It renders unconditionally as part of the module markup\n     (same JS tag gate as the rest of the card, no separate Liquid\n     check), sized larger (28px tall, 34px at >=400px container width)\n     now that it no longer has to share the row with a text wordmark.\n     The redundant \"Elite Sim Golf is an Authorized ProTee Reseller\"\n     sentence was removed from the fine print since the logo now\n     states that visually.\n     ============================================================ -->\n\n<link rel=\"preconnect\" href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com\">\n<link rel=\"preconnect\" href=\"https://fonts.gstatic.com\" crossorigin>\n<link href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Barlow+Condensed:wght@700;800&family=Inter:wght@400;500;600;700&display=swap\" rel=\"stylesheet\">\n\n<style>\n.esg-vxpromo{container-type:inline-size;margin:12px 0;box-sizing:border-box;border:1px solid #E6E9F0;background:#ffffff;position:relative}\n.esg-vxpromo *,.esg-vxpromo *::before,.esg-vxpromo *::after{box-sizing:border-box}\n\n/* --- top identity strip: Included pill (left) + reseller logo (right) --- */\n.esg-vxpromo__top{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:8px 14px;padding:9px 12px;border-bottom:1px solid #E6E9F0}\n.esg-vxpromo__reseller-logo{flex:0 0 auto;display:block;margin-left:auto;height:28px;width:auto;max-width:180px}\n.esg-vxpromo__included{position:relative;flex:0 0 auto;display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:'Barlow Condensed','Arial Narrow',sans-serif;font-size:12px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.05em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#ffffff;background:#0A1A3A;padding:4px 10px 4px 8px}\n.esg-vxpromo__included svg{flex:0 0 auto;display:block}\n\n/* --- body: 100x100 thumbnail + copy, always a slim horizontal strip\n     (this sits directly under the shipping blocks, so it should read\n     as a compact bar, not a stacked card) --- */\n.esg-vxpromo__body{display:flex;flex-direction:row;align-items:center;gap:10px;padding:8px 12px}\n.esg-vxpromo__media{flex:0 0 100px;width:100px;height:100px;background:#F8F8F8;border:1px solid #E6E9F0;overflow:hidden}\n.esg-vxpromo__media img{display:block;width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:contain;margin:0}\n.esg-vxpromo__main{flex:1 1 auto;min-width:0}\n.esg-vxpromo__eyebrow{display:block;font-family:'Barlow Condensed','Arial Narrow',sans-serif;font-size:10.5px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.09em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#3E4B7A;margin:0 0 4px}\n.esg-vxpromo__copy{font-family:'Inter',system-ui,-apple-system,sans-serif;font-size:12.5px;font-weight:400;line-height:1.45;color:#4A5578;margin:0;padding:0}\n.esg-vxpromo__copy strong{color:#0A1A3A;font-weight:700}\n.esg-vxpromo__fine{font-family:'Inter',system-ui,-apple-system,sans-serif;font-size:9.5px;font-weight:400;line-height:1.3;color:#8890A8;margin:4px 0 0;padding-top:4px;border-top:1px solid #F0F2F7}\n\n@container (min-width: 560px){\n  .esg-vxpromo__body{padding:9px 16px;gap:14px}\n}\n\n@container (min-width: 400px){\n  .esg-vxpromo__reseller-logo{height:34px;max-width:210px}\n}\n\n@container (max-width: 330px){\n  .esg-vxpromo__top{justify-content:flex-start}\n  .esg-vxpromo__reseller-logo{margin-left:0}\n}\n</style>\n\n<div class=\"esg-vxpromo\" data-esg-vxpromo data-esg-vxpromo-tag=\"ProTee VX\" style=\"display:none\">\n\n  <div class=\"esg-vxpromo__top\">\n    <span class=\"esg-vxpromo__included\">\n      <svg width=\"11\" height=\"11\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" fill=\"none\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M13.5 4L6 11.5L2.5 8\" stroke=\"#ffffff\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/></svg>\n      <span>Cameras Included</span>\n    </span>\n\n    <img class=\"esg-vxpromo__reseller-logo\" src=\"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0692/9698/0162/files/ProTee-AuthorizedReseller-DarkGreen-Transparent-US-Large.png?v=1786403473\" alt=\"ProTee Golf Authorized Reseller\" width=\"320\" height=\"120\" loading=\"lazy\">\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"esg-vxpromo__body\">\n    <span class=\"esg-vxpromo__media\">\n      <img src=\"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0692/9698/0162/files/swingcameras-proteevx_700x700_66cb5ab1-18c9-4a45-9444-89d697faddd3.png?v=1789303749\" alt=\"ProTee swing camera set included with the ProTee VX overhead launch monitor\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"100\" height=\"100\">\n    </span>\n    <div class=\"esg-vxpromo__main\">\n      <span class=\"esg-vxpromo__eyebrow\">Limited-Time Promotion · ProTee VX Swing Camera Set</span>\n      <p class=\"esg-vxpromo__copy\">Included with every ProTee VX overhead launch monitor ordered from Elite Sim Golf — a <strong>set of two ProTee swing cameras</strong>, roughly a $600 value.</p>\n      <p class=\"esg-vxpromo__fine\">While camera stock lasts. Tripods and camera mounts sold separately.</p>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n</div>\n\n<script>\n(function(){\n  // TAG GATE — only reveal the module on products tagged \"ProTee VX\"\n  // (case-insensitive, exact tag match against the storefront's public\n  // tag list). The wrapper starts with inline display:none so a slow\n  // or failed fetch never flashes the promo on the wrong product.\n  function revealIfTagged(root) {\n    var wantTag = (root.getAttribute('data-esg-vxpromo-tag') || '').trim().toLowerCase();\n    if (!wantTag) { root.style.display = ''; return; }\n\n    var handle = (window.location.pathname.match(/\\/products\\/([^/?#]+)/) || [])[1];\n    if (!handle) { return; } // not on a product page — stay hidden\n\n    fetch('/products/' + handle + '.js', { headers: { 'Accept': 'application/json' } })\n      .then(function (r) { return r.ok ? r.json() : Promise.reject(r.status); })\n      .then(function (p) {\n        var tags = (p.tags || []).map(function (t) { return String(t).trim().toLowerCase(); });\n        if (tags.indexOf(wantTag) !== -1) {\n          root.style.display = '';\n        }\n        // no match: leave hidden, don't touch layout\n      })\n      .catch(function () {\n        // Fetch failed (offline product, network hiccup, etc.) — stay\n        // hidden rather than risk showing the promo on the wrong page.\n      });\n  }\n\n  document.querySelectorAll('[data-esg-vxpromo]').forEach(revealIfTagged);\n})();\n</script>"
          }
        },
        "custom_liquid_eNw6Uh": {
          "type": "custom-liquid",
          "name": "New Universal Ship Box",
          "disabled": true,
          "settings": {
            "custom_liquid": "{%- comment -%}\n  ESG SHIPPING STATUS BOXES — condensed\n  - In-Stock: shows when total_inventory > 0\n      * Mon–Fri before 2:00 PM ET → live HH:MM:SS countdown\n      * Weekends / after Fri 2PM ET → \"Ships <next business day>\"\n  - Estimated Ship: shows when total_inventory <= 0\n      * 1–3 business day window (skips Sat/Sun)\n{%- endcomment -%}\n\n{%- assign total_inventory = 0 -%}\n{%- for variant in product.variants -%}\n  {%- assign total_inventory = total_inventory | plus: variant.inventory_quantity -%}\n{%- endfor -%}\n\n{%- if total_inventory > 0 -%}\n<div class=\"esg-shipbox\">\n  <div class=\"esg-shipbox__accent\"></div>\n\n  <div class=\"esg-shipbox__row\">\n    <span class=\"esg-shipbox__status\">\n      <svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M20 6L9 17l-5-5\"></path></svg>\n      In Stock • Ready to Ship\n    </span>\n  </div>\n\n  <div id=\"esg-2pm-countdown-wrap\" class=\"esg-shipbox__countdown\">\n    <div class=\"esg-shipbox__countdown-copy\">\n      <div class=\"esg-shipbox__cutoff-label\" id=\"esg-cutoff-label\">Same-Day Shipping Cutoff</div>\n      <div class=\"esg-shipbox__cutoff-sub\" id=\"esg-cutoff-sub\">Order by <strong>2:00 PM ET</strong></div>\n    </div>\n    <div id=\"esg-2pm-time\" class=\"esg-shipbox__clock\">--:--:--</div>\n  </div>\n</div>\n\n<script>\n(function () {\n  var wrap = document.getElementById('esg-2pm-countdown-wrap');\n  var timeEl = document.getElementById('esg-2pm-time');\n  var labelEl = document.getElementById('esg-cutoff-label');\n  var subEl = document.getElementById('esg-cutoff-sub');\n  if (!wrap || !timeEl) return;\n\n  function pad(n) { return String(n).padStart(2, '0'); }\n  function getETParts(d) {\n    var out = {};\n    new Intl.DateTimeFormat('en-US', {\n      timeZone: 'America/New_York',\n      hour: '2-digit', minute: '2-digit', second: '2-digit', hour12: false\n    }).formatToParts(d).forEach(function (p) { out[p.type] = p.value; });\n    return out;\n  }\n  function getETDow(d) {\n    var wk = new Intl.DateTimeFormat('en-US', { timeZone: 'America/New_York', weekday: 'short' }).format(d);\n    return ({Sun:0,Mon:1,Tue:2,Wed:3,Thu:4,Fri:5,Sat:6})[wk];\n  }\n  function formatET(date, opts) {\n    return new Intl.DateTimeFormat('en-US', Object.assign({ timeZone: 'America/New_York' }, opts)).format(date);\n  }\n  // Find the next ET business day (Mon–Fri) after `from`\n  function nextBusinessDay(from) {\n    for (var i = 1; i <= 7; i++) {\n      var d = new Date(from.getTime() + i * 86400000);\n      var dow = getETDow(d);\n      if (dow !== 0 && dow !== 6) return d;\n    }\n    return null;\n  }\n  function update() {\n    var now = new Date();\n    var p = getETParts(now);\n    var dow = getETDow(now);\n    var nowSec = parseInt(p.hour,10)*3600 + parseInt(p.minute,10)*60 + parseInt(p.second,10);\n    var cutoffSec = 14 * 3600;\n    var closed = (dow === 0 || dow === 6) || nowSec >= cutoffSec;\n\n    if (closed) {\n      var nb = nextBusinessDay(now);\n      var weekday  = nb ? formatET(nb, { weekday: 'long' })  : 'next business day';\n      var dateLong = nb ? formatET(nb, { month: 'long', day: 'numeric' }) : '';\n      var dateShort = nb ? formatET(nb, { month: 'short', day: 'numeric' }) : '';\n      labelEl.textContent = 'Ships Next Business Day';\n      subEl.innerHTML = '<strong>' + weekday + (dateLong ? ', ' + dateLong : '') + '</strong>';\n      timeEl.innerHTML = '<span class=\"esg-shipbox__clock-day\">' + weekday.toUpperCase() + '</span><span class=\"esg-shipbox__clock-date\">' + dateShort.toUpperCase() + '</span>';\n      timeEl.classList.add('esg-shipbox__clock--text');\n      return;\n    }\n    labelEl.textContent = 'Same-Day Shipping Cutoff';\n    subEl.innerHTML = 'Order by <strong>2:00 PM ET</strong>';\n    timeEl.classList.remove('esg-shipbox__clock--text');\n    var r = cutoffSec - nowSec;\n    timeEl.textContent = pad(Math.floor(r/3600)) + ':' + pad(Math.floor((r%3600)/60)) + ':' + pad(r%60);\n  }\n  update();\n  setInterval(update, 1000);\n})();\n</script>\n{%- endif -%}\n\n\n{%- if total_inventory <= 0 -%}\n  {%- assign one_day = 86400 -%}\n  {%- assign today_ts = 'now' | date: '%s' | plus: 0 -%}\n  {%- assign business_days_found = 0 -%}\n  {%- assign ship_start_ts = blank -%}\n  {%- assign ship_end_ts = blank -%}\n\n  {%- for i in (1..7) -%}\n    {%- assign add = one_day | times: i -%}\n    {%- assign check_ts = today_ts | plus: add -%}\n    {%- assign check_day = check_ts | date: '%u' | plus: 0 -%}\n    {%- unless check_day == 6 or check_day == 7 -%}\n      {%- assign business_days_found = business_days_found | plus: 1 -%}\n      {%- if business_days_found == 1 -%}{%- assign ship_start_ts = check_ts -%}{%- endif -%}\n      {%- if business_days_found == 3 -%}{%- assign ship_end_ts = check_ts -%}{%- break -%}{%- endif -%}\n    {%- endunless -%}\n  {%- endfor -%}\n\n  <div class=\"esg-shipest\">\n    <div class=\"esg-shipest__accent\"></div>\n    <div class=\"esg-shipest__icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n      <svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.9\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"9\"></circle><path d=\"M12 7v5l3 2\"></path></svg>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"esg-shipest__content\">\n      <div class=\"esg-shipest__label\">Estimated Ship Date</div>\n      <div class=\"esg-shipest__dates\">{{ ship_start_ts | date: '%a %b %-d' }} — {{ ship_end_ts | date: '%a %b %-d' }}</div>\n      <div class=\"esg-shipest__sub\">Typically 1–3 business days.</div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n{%- endif -%}\n\n<style>\n  .esg-shipbox, .esg-shipest {\n    max-width: 1100px;\n    margin: 10px 0;\n    position: relative;\n    overflow: hidden;\n    border: 1px solid #e5e7eb;\n    border-radius: 16px;\n    background: #ffffff;\n    box-shadow: 0 8px 20px rgba(15, 23, 42, .05);\n    color: #2a3756;\n    font-family: inherit;\n    line-height: 1.35;\n  }\n  .esg-shipbox__accent, .esg-shipest__accent {\n    position: absolute; inset: 0 0 auto; height: 3px;\n    background: linear-gradient(90deg, #086ED3 0%, #0A1A3A 100%);\n  }\n\n  /* In-stock box */\n  .esg-shipbox { padding: 10px 12px 11px; }\n  .esg-shipbox__row { margin-bottom: 8px; }\n  .esg-shipbox__status {\n    display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 6px;\n    padding: 5px 10px; border-radius: 999px;\n    background: #ecfdf3; border: 1px solid #bbf7d0; color: #15803d;\n    font-family: 'Barlow Condensed', 'Barlow', sans-serif;\n    font-size: 12px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: .1em;\n    text-transform: uppercase; line-height: 1; white-space: nowrap;\n  }\n  .esg-shipbox__status svg { width: 11px; height: 11px; }\n\n  .esg-shipbox__countdown {\n    padding: 8px 11px; border-radius: 10px;\n    border: 1px solid rgba(8, 110, 211, .18); background: #ffffff;\n    display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between;\n    gap: 10px; flex-wrap: wrap;\n    box-shadow: 0 2px 6px rgba(8, 110, 211, .06);\n  }\n  .esg-shipbox__countdown-copy { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 2px; }\n  .esg-shipbox__cutoff-label {\n    font-family: 'Barlow Condensed', 'Barlow', sans-serif;\n    font-size: 11px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: .14em;\n    text-transform: uppercase; color: #086ED3; line-height: 1;\n  }\n  .esg-shipbox__cutoff-sub { font-size: 12.5px; color: #2a3756; font-weight: 500; }\n  .esg-shipbox__cutoff-sub strong { color: #0A1A3A; font-weight: 700; }\n\n  .esg-shipbox__clock {\n    display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;\n    min-width: 130px; padding: 6px 12px; border-radius: 7px;\n    background: linear-gradient(180deg, #0A1A3A 0%, #071a33 100%);\n    color: #ffffff; font-weight: 800; font-size: 18px;\n    letter-spacing: .12em; line-height: 1;\n    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;\n    font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Monaco, Consolas, 'Liberation Mono', 'Courier New', monospace;\n    box-shadow: inset 0 2px 4px rgba(0,0,0,.25), 0 2px 6px rgba(10, 26, 58, .25);\n    border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, .08);\n  }\n  .esg-shipbox__clock--text {\n    flex-direction: column; gap: 2px;\n    padding: 8px 14px;\n    font-family: 'Barlow Condensed', 'Barlow', sans-serif;\n    letter-spacing: .12em; line-height: 1.05;\n  }\n  .esg-shipbox__clock-day {\n    font-size: 15px; font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: .14em;\n  }\n  .esg-shipbox__clock-date {\n    font-size: 12px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: .14em;\n    color: rgba(255,255,255,.85);\n  }\n\n  /* Estimated ship box */\n  .esg-shipest {\n    padding: 9px 12px; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px;\n  }\n  .esg-shipest__icon {\n    display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;\n    width: 34px; height: 34px; min-width: 34px; border-radius: 9px;\n    background: #ffffff; color: #086ED3;\n    border: 1px solid rgba(8, 110, 211, .18);\n    box-shadow: 0 2px 6px rgba(8, 110, 211, .08);\n    flex: 0 0 auto;\n  }\n  .esg-shipest__icon svg { width: 18px; height: 18px; display: block; }\n  .esg-shipest__content { min-width: 0; line-height: 1.3; }\n  .esg-shipest__label {\n    font-family: 'Barlow Condensed', 'Barlow', sans-serif;\n    font-size: 11px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: .14em;\n    text-transform: uppercase; color: #086ED3; margin-bottom: 1px;\n  }\n  .esg-shipest__dates {\n    font-family: 'Barlow Condensed', 'Barlow', sans-serif;\n    font-size: 15px; font-weight: 800; color: #0A1A3A;\n    letter-spacing: .02em; text-transform: uppercase; line-height: 1.15;\n  }\n  .esg-shipest__sub { font-size: 12px; color: #2a3756; line-height: 1.35; }\n\n  @media (max-width: 749px) {\n    .esg-shipbox, .esg-shipest { border-radius: 14px; }\n    .esg-shipbox { padding: 9px 11px 10px; }\n    .esg-shipbox__cutoff-label { font-size: 10.5px; }\n    .esg-shipbox__cutoff-sub { font-size: 12px; }\n    .esg-shipbox__clock { min-width: 118px; font-size: 16px; padding: 6px 10px; }\n    .esg-shipbox__clock--text { padding: 7px 12px; }\n    .esg-shipbox__clock-day { font-size: 13px; }\n    .esg-shipbox__clock-date { font-size: 11px; }\n    .esg-shipest { padding: 9px 11px; }\n    .esg-shipest__icon { width: 30px; height: 30px; min-width: 30px; }\n    .esg-shipest__icon svg { width: 16px; height: 16px; }\n    .esg-shipest__dates { font-size: 14px; }\n  }\n</style>"
          }
        },
        "custom_liquid_LWnqjF": {
          "type": "custom-liquid",
          "name": "Projector Fitment",
          "disabled": true,
          "settings": {
            "custom_liquid": "{%- if product.type == 'Projector' -%}\n\n{%- comment -%}\n  =========================================================\n  ESG Projector Fitment Box\n  ---------------------------------------------------------\n  Reads product TAGS (populate per projector in Shopify admin):\n\n    throw:1.20-1.80     (required — min/max throw ratio)\n    throw:1.50          (also valid for fixed-throw projectors)\n    aspect:16:9         (optional — defaults to 16:9)\n\n  User enters viewable SCREEN HEIGHT. Width is derived from\n  the aspect ratio, then throw distance is calculated as\n  width × throw_ratio.\n\n  If no throw tag is found, falls back to the static\n  \"Check Fitment\" CTA (no calculator).\n  =========================================================\n{%- endcomment -%}\n\n{%- assign tr_min = 0 -%}\n{%- assign tr_max = 0 -%}\n{%- assign aspect = '16:9' -%}\n{%- assign min_height = 72 -%}\n{%- assign max_height = 144 -%}\n{%- assign default_height = 96 -%}\n\n{%- comment -%} Parse tags: throw:X.XX-Y.YY  |  throw:X.XX  |  aspect:W:H {%- endcomment -%}\n{%- for raw_tag in product.tags -%}\n  {%- assign tag = raw_tag | downcase | strip -%}\n\n  {%- if tag contains 'throw:' -%}\n    {%- assign throw_val = tag | remove_first: 'throw:' | strip -%}\n    {%- if throw_val contains '-' -%}\n      {%- assign throw_parts = throw_val | split: '-' -%}\n      {%- assign tr_min = throw_parts[0] | strip | plus: 0.0 -%}\n      {%- assign tr_max = throw_parts[1] | strip | plus: 0.0 -%}\n    {%- else -%}\n      {%- assign tr_min = throw_val | plus: 0.0 -%}\n      {%- assign tr_max = throw_val | plus: 0.0 -%}\n    {%- endif -%}\n  {%- endif -%}\n\n  {%- if tag contains 'aspect:' -%}\n    {%- assign aspect = tag | remove_first: 'aspect:' | strip -%}\n  {%- endif -%}\n{%- endfor -%}\n\n{%- assign has_throw_data = false -%}\n{%- if tr_min > 0 and tr_max > 0 -%}\n  {%- assign has_throw_data = true -%}\n{%- endif -%}\n\n<div class=\"esg-projector-fit\"\n     data-throw-min=\"{{ tr_min }}\"\n     data-throw-max=\"{{ tr_max }}\"\n     data-aspect=\"{{ aspect | escape }}\"\n     data-min-height=\"{{ min_height }}\"\n     data-max-height=\"{{ max_height }}\"\n     data-default-height=\"{{ default_height }}\">\n  <div class=\"esg-projector-fit__accent\"></div>\n\n  <div class=\"esg-projector-fit__body\">\n    <div class=\"esg-projector-fit__icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n      <svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.9\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">\n        <path d=\"M15 3h6v6\"></path>\n        <path d=\"M9 21H3v-6\"></path>\n        <path d=\"M21 3l-7 7\"></path>\n        <path d=\"M3 21l7-7\"></path>\n      </svg>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"esg-projector-fit__content\">\n      <div class=\"esg-projector-fit__eyebrow\">Projector Fitment</div>\n      <h3 class=\"esg-projector-fit__title\">Will This Projector Fit My Space?</h3>\n\n      {%- if has_throw_data -%}\n        <div class=\"esg-projector-fit__specs\">\n          <span class=\"esg-projector-fit__spec\"><strong>Throw ratio:</strong> {{ tr_min }}–{{ tr_max }}</span>\n          <span class=\"esg-projector-fit__spec-sep\">·</span>\n          <span class=\"esg-projector-fit__spec\"><strong>Native aspect:</strong> {{ aspect }}</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"esg-projector-fit__text\">\n          Enter your viewable screen height to estimate how far back this projector needs to mount.\n        </div>\n      {%- else -%}\n        <div class=\"esg-projector-fit__text\">\n          Use our projector fitment tool to check screen size, aspect ratio, and mounting distance before you buy.\n        </div>\n      {%- endif -%}\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  {%- if has_throw_data -%}\n    <div class=\"esg-projector-fit__calc\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"Mini fitment calculator\">\n      <label class=\"esg-projector-fit__field\">\n        <span class=\"esg-projector-fit__field-label\">Viewable Screen Height</span>\n        <span class=\"esg-projector-fit__input-wrap\">\n          <input type=\"number\"\n                 class=\"esg-projector-fit__input\"\n                 min=\"{{ min_height }}\"\n                 max=\"{{ max_height }}\"\n                 step=\"1\"\n                 value=\"{{ default_height }}\"\n                 inputmode=\"numeric\"\n                 aria-label=\"Viewable screen height in inches\">\n          <span class=\"esg-projector-fit__unit\">in</span>\n        </span>\n        <span class=\"esg-projector-fit__field-hint\" data-width-hint>Screen width: —</span>\n      </label>\n\n      <div class=\"esg-projector-fit__result\">\n        <div class=\"esg-projector-fit__result-label\">Throw Distance</div>\n        <div class=\"esg-projector-fit__result-value\" data-result>—</div>\n        <div class=\"esg-projector-fit__result-sub\" data-result-sub>From screen to lens</div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"esg-projector-fit__footer\">\n      <span class=\"esg-projector-fit__disclaimer\">Estimate only · Lens shift &amp; zoom not factored in.</span>\n      <a href=\"/pages/projector-fitment-tool-and-throw-calculator\" class=\"esg-projector-fit__link\">\n        Full fitment tool\n        <svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n          <path d=\"M5 12h14\"></path>\n          <path d=\"m12 5 7 7-7 7\"></path>\n        </svg>\n      </a>\n    </div>\n  {%- else -%}\n    <a href=\"/pages/projector-fitment-tool-and-throw-calculator\" class=\"esg-projector-fit__button\">\n      <span>Check Fitment</span>\n      <svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n        <path d=\"M5 12h14\"></path>\n        <path d=\"m12 5 7 7-7 7\"></path>\n      </svg>\n    </a>\n  {%- endif -%}\n</div>\n\n{%- if has_throw_data -%}\n<script>\n(function() {\n  var root = document.currentScript.previousElementSibling;\n  while (root && !root.classList.contains('esg-projector-fit')) {\n    root = root.previousElementSibling;\n  }\n  if (!root) return;\n\n  var input = root.querySelector('.esg-projector-fit__input');\n  var resultEl = root.querySelector('[data-result]');\n  var resultSubEl = root.querySelector('[data-result-sub]');\n  var widthHintEl = root.querySelector('[data-width-hint]');\n  if (!input || !resultEl) return;\n\n  var trMin = parseFloat(root.dataset.throwMin);\n  var trMax = parseFloat(root.dataset.throwMax);\n  var minH  = parseFloat(root.dataset.minHeight);\n  var maxH  = parseFloat(root.dataset.maxHeight);\n\n  var aspectParts = (root.dataset.aspect || '16:9').split(':');\n  var aspectW = parseFloat(aspectParts[0]) || 16;\n  var aspectH = parseFloat(aspectParts[1]) || 9;\n  var aspectRatio = aspectW / aspectH; // width per unit of height\n\n  function inchesToFtIn(inches) {\n    var totalIn = Math.round(inches);\n    var ft = Math.floor(totalIn / 12);\n    var rem = totalIn % 12;\n    return ft + \"' \" + rem + '\"';\n  }\n\n  function update() {\n    var h = parseFloat(input.value);\n    if (isNaN(h) || h < minH || h > maxH) {\n      resultEl.textContent = '—';\n      resultSubEl.textContent = 'Enter a screen height between ' + minH + '\" and ' + maxH + '\"';\n      if (widthHintEl) widthHintEl.textContent = 'Screen width: —';\n      return;\n    }\n\n    // Derive viewable screen width from height + native aspect ratio\n    var w = h * aspectRatio;\n    if (widthHintEl) {\n      widthHintEl.textContent = 'Screen width: ' + inchesToFtIn(w) + ' (' + aspectW + ':' + aspectH + ')';\n    }\n\n    var minDist = w * trMin; // inches\n    var maxDist = w * trMax;\n    if (Math.abs(maxDist - minDist) < 0.5) {\n      resultEl.textContent = inchesToFtIn(minDist);\n      resultSubEl.textContent = 'Fixed throw distance from screen';\n    } else {\n      resultEl.textContent = inchesToFtIn(minDist) + ' – ' + inchesToFtIn(maxDist);\n      resultSubEl.textContent = 'Range based on zoom from screen to lens';\n    }\n  }\n\n  input.addEventListener('input', update);\n  input.addEventListener('change', update);\n  update();\n})();\n</script>\n{%- endif -%}\n\n<style>\n  .esg-projector-fit {\n    max-width: 1100px;\n    margin: 12px 0;\n    position: relative;\n    overflow: hidden;\n    padding: 14px 16px;\n    border: 1px solid #e5e7eb;\n    border-radius: 14px;\n    background: linear-gradient(180deg, #ffffff 0%, #f8fbff 100%);\n    box-shadow: 0 6px 16px rgba(15, 23, 42, .04);\n    color: #2a3756;\n    font-family: inherit;\n    line-height: 1.4;\n    display: flex;\n    flex-direction: column;\n    gap: 12px;\n  }\n\n  .esg-projector-fit__accent {\n    position: absolute;\n    inset: 0 0 auto;\n    height: 3px;\n    background: linear-gradient(90deg, #086ED3 0%, #0A1A3A 100%);\n  }\n\n  .esg-projector-fit__body {\n    display: flex;\n    align-items: center;\n    gap: 12px;\n    min-width: 0;\n  }\n\n  .esg-projector-fit__icon {\n    display: inline-flex;\n    align-items: center;\n    justify-content: center;\n    width: 44px;\n    height: 44px;\n    min-width: 44px;\n    border-radius: 12px;\n    background: #ffffff;\n    color: #086ED3;\n    border: 1px solid rgba(8, 110, 211, .18);\n    box-shadow: 0 2px 6px rgba(8, 110, 211, .08);\n    flex: 0 0 auto;\n  }\n  .esg-projector-fit__icon svg { width: 22px; height: 22px; display: block; }\n\n  .esg-projector-fit__content { min-width: 0; flex: 1; }\n\n  .esg-projector-fit__eyebrow {\n    font-family: 'Barlow Condensed', 'Barlow', sans-serif;\n    font-size: 11.5px;\n    font-weight: 700;\n    letter-spacing: .16em;\n    text-transform: uppercase;\n    color: #086ED3;\n    line-height: 1;\n    margin-bottom: 4px;\n  }\n\n  .esg-projector-fit__title {\n    margin: 0 0 4px;\n    color: #0A1A3A;\n    font-family: 'Barlow Condensed', 'Barlow', sans-serif;\n    font-size: 17px;\n    font-weight: 800;\n    letter-spacing: .02em;\n    text-transform: uppercase;\n    line-height: 1.15;\n  }\n\n  .esg-projector-fit__specs {\n    display: flex;\n    flex-wrap: wrap;\n    align-items: center;\n    gap: 4px 8px;\n    margin-bottom: 4px;\n    font-size: 12.5px;\n    color: #2a3756;\n  }\n  .esg-projector-fit__spec strong { color: #0A1A3A; font-weight: 700; }\n  .esg-projector-fit__spec-sep { color: rgba(8, 110, 211, .45); }\n\n  .esg-projector-fit__text {\n    font-size: 12.5px;\n    color: #2a3756;\n    line-height: 1.4;\n  }\n\n  /* ----- Mini calculator ----- */\n  .esg-projector-fit__calc {\n    display: grid;\n    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1.4fr);\n    gap: 10px;\n    padding: 12px;\n    border-radius: 12px;\n    border: 1px solid rgba(8, 110, 211, .18);\n    background: #ffffff;\n    box-shadow: 0 2px 6px rgba(8, 110, 211, .06);\n  }\n\n  .esg-projector-fit__field {\n    display: flex;\n    flex-direction: column;\n    min-width: 0;\n  }\n\n  .esg-projector-fit__field-label {\n    font-family: 'Barlow Condensed', 'Barlow', sans-serif;\n    font-size: 11.5px;\n    font-weight: 700;\n    letter-spacing: .14em;\n    text-transform: uppercase;\n    color: #086ED3;\n    line-height: 1;\n    margin-bottom: 6px;\n  }\n\n  .esg-projector-fit__field-hint {\n    margin-top: 6px;\n    font-size: 11.5px;\n    color: #6B7390;\n    line-height: 1.3;\n  }\n\n  .esg-projector-fit__input-wrap {\n    position: relative;\n    display: flex;\n    align-items: stretch;\n  }\n\n  .esg-projector-fit__input {\n    flex: 1;\n    min-width: 0;\n    height: 42px;\n    padding: 0 38px 0 12px;\n    border: 1px solid #d8e3f0;\n    border-radius: 10px;\n    background: #f8fbff;\n    color: #0A1A3A;\n    font-family: 'Barlow Condensed', 'Barlow', sans-serif;\n    font-size: 20px;\n    font-weight: 800;\n    letter-spacing: .02em;\n    line-height: 1;\n    appearance: textfield;\n    -moz-appearance: textfield;\n    transition: border-color .15s ease, box-shadow .15s ease, background .15s ease;\n  }\n  .esg-projector-fit__input::-webkit-outer-spin-button,\n  .esg-projector-fit__input::-webkit-inner-spin-button { -webkit-appearance: none; margin: 0; }\n  .esg-projector-fit__input:focus {\n    outline: none;\n    border-color: #086ED3;\n    background: #ffffff;\n    box-shadow: 0 0 0 3px rgba(8, 110, 211, .15);\n  }\n\n  .esg-projector-fit__unit {\n    position: absolute;\n    right: 12px;\n    top: 50%;\n    transform: translateY(-50%);\n    font-family: 'Barlow Condensed', 'Barlow', sans-serif;\n    font-size: 13px;\n    font-weight: 700;\n    letter-spacing: .08em;\n    text-transform: uppercase;\n    color: #086ED3;\n    pointer-events: none;\n  }\n\n  .esg-projector-fit__result {\n    display: flex;\n    flex-direction: column;\n    justify-content: center;\n    padding: 6px 14px;\n    border-radius: 10px;\n    background: linear-gradient(180deg, #0A1A3A 0%, #071a33 100%);\n    color: #ffffff;\n    min-width: 0;\n  }\n\n  .esg-projector-fit__result-label {\n    font-family: 'Barlow Condensed', 'Barlow', sans-serif;\n    font-size: 11px;\n    font-weight: 700;\n    letter-spacing: .16em;\n    text-transform: uppercase;\n    color: #C9D6F2;\n    line-height: 1;\n    margin-bottom: 4px;\n  }\n\n  .esg-projector-fit__result-value {\n    font-family: 'Barlow Condensed', 'Barlow', sans-serif;\n    font-size: 22px;\n    font-weight: 800;\n    letter-spacing: .02em;\n    line-height: 1.1;\n    color: #ffffff;\n    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;\n  }\n\n  .esg-projector-fit__result-sub {\n    font-size: 11.5px;\n    color: #C9D6F2;\n    line-height: 1.3;\n    margin-top: 2px;\n  }\n\n  .esg-projector-fit__footer {\n    display: flex;\n    align-items: center;\n    justify-content: space-between;\n    gap: 10px;\n    flex-wrap: wrap;\n  }\n\n  .esg-projector-fit__disclaimer {\n    font-size: 11.5px;\n    color: #6B7390;\n    line-height: 1.3;\n  }\n\n  .esg-projector-fit__link {\n    display: inline-flex;\n    align-items: center;\n    gap: 6px;\n    color: #086ED3;\n    font-family: 'Barlow Condensed', 'Barlow', sans-serif;\n    font-size: 13px;\n    font-weight: 800;\n    letter-spacing: .08em;\n    text-transform: uppercase;\n    text-decoration: none;\n    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(8, 110, 211, .35);\n    padding-bottom: 1px;\n  }\n  .esg-projector-fit__link:hover { border-bottom-color: #086ED3; color: #086ED3; }\n  .esg-projector-fit__link svg { width: 12px; height: 12px; transition: transform .15s ease; }\n  .esg-projector-fit__link:hover svg { transform: translateX(3px); }\n\n  /* ----- Fallback CTA (no throw tag) ----- */\n  .esg-projector-fit__button {\n    align-self: flex-start;\n    display: inline-flex;\n    align-items: center;\n    justify-content: center;\n    gap: 8px;\n    text-decoration: none;\n    border: 1px solid #086ED3;\n    border-radius: 999px;\n    padding: 11px 20px;\n    background: linear-gradient(180deg, #086ED3 0%, #075cb3 100%);\n    color: #ffffff;\n    font-family: 'Barlow Condensed', 'Barlow', sans-serif;\n    font-size: 14px;\n    font-weight: 800;\n    letter-spacing: .08em;\n    text-transform: uppercase;\n    line-height: 1;\n    box-shadow: 0 4px 10px rgba(8, 110, 211, .25);\n    transition: transform .15s ease, box-shadow .15s ease, background .15s ease;\n    white-space: nowrap;\n  }\n  .esg-projector-fit__button:hover,\n  .esg-projector-fit__button:focus {\n    background: linear-gradient(180deg, #0A1A3A 0%, #071a33 100%);\n    transform: translateY(-1px);\n    box-shadow: 0 6px 14px rgba(10, 26, 58, .3);\n    color: #ffffff;\n    border-color: #0A1A3A;\n  }\n  .esg-projector-fit__button svg { width: 14px; height: 14px; transition: transform .15s ease; }\n  .esg-projector-fit__button:hover svg { transform: translateX(3px); }\n\n  /* ----- Mobile ----- */\n  @media (max-width: 749px) {\n    .esg-projector-fit { padding: 13px 14px; border-radius: 12px; gap: 11px; }\n    .esg-projector-fit__body { gap: 11px; }\n    .esg-projector-fit__icon {\n      width: 38px; height: 38px; min-width: 38px; border-radius: 10px;\n    }\n    .esg-projector-fit__icon svg { width: 20px; height: 20px; }\n    .esg-projector-fit__title { font-size: 16px; }\n    .esg-projector-fit__text, .esg-projector-fit__specs { font-size: 12.5px; }\n\n    .esg-projector-fit__calc {\n      grid-template-columns: 1fr;\n      padding: 11px;\n      gap: 10px;\n    }\n    .esg-projector-fit__input { height: 44px; font-size: 18px; }\n    .esg-projector-fit__result-value { font-size: 20px; }\n\n    .esg-projector-fit__button {\n      width: 100%;\n      padding: 12px 18px;\n      align-self: stretch;\n    }\n\n    .esg-projector-fit__footer {\n      flex-direction: column;\n      align-items: flex-start;\n      gap: 6px;\n    }\n  }\n</style>\n{%- endif -%}"
          }
        },
        "buy-buttons": {
          "type": "buy-buttons",
          "settings": {
            "show_qty_selector": true,
            "enable_dynamic_checkout": true,
            "show_pickup_availability": true,
            "show_backorder_text": false,
            "show_gift_card_recipient": false,
            "show_inventory_notice": "never",
            "show_inventory_count": "never",
            "inventory_threshold": 1
          }
        },
        "custom_liquid_k3xdLk": {
          "type": "custom-liquid",
          "name": "Custom Accessories",
          "settings": {
            "custom_liquid": "{%- comment -%}\n============================================================\n  ESG ACCESSORIES -- INLINE VERSION\n  Paste this whole thing into the Custom Liquid block on the\n  ProTee VX product template. No esg-accessories snippet needed.\n  Still requires snippets/esg-acc-row.liquid (already saved).\n\n  Heading resolves automatically from the product:\n    'acc-label:<value>' tag  ->  longest tag matching the start\n    of the title  ->  vendor  ->  'Popular Accessories'\n============================================================\n{%- endcomment -%}\n\n{%- liquid\n  assign uid = 'esgacc-' | append: product.id\n\n  assign esg_label = ''\n\n  if esg_label == ''\n    for t in product.tags\n      assign t_low = t | downcase\n      if t_low contains 'acc-label:'\n        assign esg_label = t | split: ':' | last | strip\n        break\n      endif\n    endfor\n  endif\n\n  if esg_label == ''\n    assign best = ''\n    assign title_len = product.title | size\n    for t in product.tags\n      assign t_len = t | size\n      if t_len > 0 and t_len <= title_len\n        assign head = product.title | slice: 0, t_len\n        if head == t\n          assign best_len = best | size\n          if t_len > best_len\n            assign best = t\n          endif\n        endif\n      endif\n    endfor\n    assign esg_label = best\n  endif\n\n  if esg_label == ''\n    assign esg_label = product.vendor | default: ''\n  endif\n\n  assign heading_pattern = 'Popular [label] Accessories'\n\n  if esg_label == ''\n    assign heading_text = 'Popular Accessories'\n  else\n    assign heading_text = heading_pattern | replace: '[label]', esg_label\n  endif\n\n\n  assign sub_text = ''\n  if sub_text == ''\n    if esg_label == ''\n      assign sub_text = '[count] add-on[s] buyers order most'\n    else\n      assign sub_text = '[count] add-on[s] [label] buyers order most'\n    endif\n  endif\n  assign handles_str = ''\n  assign max = 24\n  assign visible = 3\n\n  # ----------------------------------------------------------\n  # DEFAULT SET (fallback)\n  # Used only when a launch monitor product has no complementary\n  # products assigned in Search & Discovery. Edit this one line to\n  # change what shows: comma separated product handles, in order.\n  # Keep it to generic add-ons that suit ANY launch monitor -- model\n  # specific items belong on that model's own complementary list.\n  # ----------------------------------------------------------\n  assign fallback_handles = 'gspro-golf-simulator-software-1-year-subscription,golf-simulator-pc-add-on-surfthing-sg3-series,golf-simulator-gaming-desktop-pc-all-configurations-by-elite-sim-golf'\n\n  # Gate: launch monitor product pages only. The substring test is\n  # deliberate -- the real type on these products is 'Golf Launch\n  # Monitor', not 'Launch Monitor', so an exact match never fires.\n  # Accessory and protection types contain the same substring, so\n  # they are excluded: a case or shield PDP is not a launch monitor.\n  assign type_low = product.type | default: '' | downcase\n  assign type_ok = false\n  if type_low contains 'launch monitor'\n    assign type_ok = true\n    if type_low contains 'accessor'\n      assign type_ok = false\n    endif\n    if type_low contains 'protection'\n      assign type_ok = false\n    endif\n  endif\n\n  # Count assigned complementary products that would actually render.\n  # Unpublished or deleted references come back nil, so a non-empty\n  # metafield can still produce zero rows -- count the usable ones.\n  assign complementary = product.metafields.shopify--discovery--product_recommendation.complementary_products.value\n  assign comp_valid = 0\n  for cp in complementary limit: max\n    if cp != blank and cp.handle != product.handle\n      assign comp_valid = comp_valid | plus: 1\n    endif\n  endfor\n\n  assign use_fallback = false\n  if comp_valid == 0 and type_ok and fallback_handles != ''\n    assign use_fallback = true\n  endif\n\n  # all_products is capped at 20 lookups per template by Shopify, so the\n  # handle driven paths stay well under it.\n  assign fb_max = 12\n  assign visible_plus = visible | plus: 1\n  assign is_open = true\n  assign n = 0\n-%}\n\n{%- comment -%} Resolve which products to show {%- endcomment -%}\n{%- capture rows -%}\n  {%- if handles_str != '' -%}\n    {%- assign handle_list = handles_str | split: ',' -%}\n    {%- for h in handle_list -%}\n      {%- assign key = h | strip -%}\n      {%- assign p = all_products[key] -%}\n      {%- if p != blank and p.id != blank and p.handle != product.handle -%}\n        {%- assign n = n | plus: 1 -%}\n        {%- if n == visible_plus -%}<details class=\"esg-acc-more\"><summary class=\"esg-acc-more__sum\"><span class=\"esg-acc-more__txt esg-acc-more__txt--closed\">Show [MORE] more</span><span class=\"esg-acc-more__txt esg-acc-more__txt--open\">Show less</span><span class=\"esg-acc-more__chev\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span></summary><div class=\"esg-acc-more__body\">{%- endif -%}\n        {%- render 'esg-acc-row', p: p -%}\n      {%- endif -%}\n    {%- endfor -%}\n  {%- elsif use_fallback -%}\n    {%- assign fb_list = fallback_handles | split: ',' -%}\n    {%- for h in fb_list limit: fb_max -%}\n      {%- assign key = h | strip -%}\n      {%- assign p = all_products[key] -%}\n      {%- if p != blank and p.id != blank and p.handle != product.handle -%}\n        {%- assign n = n | plus: 1 -%}\n        {%- if n == visible_plus -%}<details class=\"esg-acc-more\"><summary class=\"esg-acc-more__sum\"><span class=\"esg-acc-more__txt esg-acc-more__txt--closed\">Show [MORE] more</span><span class=\"esg-acc-more__txt esg-acc-more__txt--open\">Show less</span><span class=\"esg-acc-more__chev\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span></summary><div class=\"esg-acc-more__body\">{%- endif -%}\n        {%- render 'esg-acc-row', p: p -%}\n      {%- endif -%}\n    {%- endfor -%}\n  {%- else -%}\n    {%- for p in complementary limit: max -%}\n      {%- if p != blank and p.handle != product.handle -%}\n        {%- assign n = n | plus: 1 -%}\n        {%- if n == visible_plus -%}<details class=\"esg-acc-more\"><summary class=\"esg-acc-more__sum\"><span class=\"esg-acc-more__txt esg-acc-more__txt--closed\">Show [MORE] more</span><span class=\"esg-acc-more__txt esg-acc-more__txt--open\">Show less</span><span class=\"esg-acc-more__chev\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span></summary><div class=\"esg-acc-more__body\">{%- endif -%}\n        {%- render 'esg-acc-row', p: p -%}\n      {%- endif -%}\n    {%- endfor -%}\n  {%- endif -%}\n{%- endcapture -%}\n\n{%- assign row_count = rows | split: 'data-esg-row' | size | minus: 1 -%}\n\n{%- if row_count > visible -%}\n  {%- assign extra = row_count | minus: visible -%}\n  {%- assign rows = rows | append: '</div></details>' | replace: '[MORE]', extra -%}\n{%- endif -%}\n\n{%- if row_count > 0 -%}\n<link rel=\"preconnect\" href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com\">\n<link rel=\"preconnect\" href=\"https://fonts.gstatic.com\" crossorigin>\n<link href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Barlow+Condensed:wght@700;800&family=Inter:wght@400;500;600&display=swap\" rel=\"stylesheet\">\n\n<style>\n  .esg-acc-wrap{container-type:inline-size;margin:0;box-sizing:border-box}\n  .esg-acc-wrap *,.esg-acc-wrap *::before,.esg-acc-wrap *::after{box-sizing:border-box}\n  .esg-acc-wrap .esg-acc{border:1px solid #E6E9F0;border-top:3px solid #0A1A3A;background:#fff;margin:0}\n  .esg-acc-wrap .esg-acc__sum{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:10px;padding:14px 16px;cursor:pointer;list-style:none;background:#F8F8F8;transition:background .15s ease}\n  .esg-acc-wrap .esg-acc__sum::-webkit-details-marker{display:none}\n  .esg-acc-wrap .esg-acc__sum::marker{content:\"\"}\n  .esg-acc-wrap .esg-acc__sum:hover{background:#F1F3F7}\n  .esg-acc-wrap .esg-acc__sum-txt{min-width:0}\n  .esg-acc-wrap .esg-acc__label{display:block;font-family:'Barlow Condensed','Arial Narrow',sans-serif;font-size:17px;font-weight:800;line-height:1.15;letter-spacing:.01em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#0A1A3A}\n  .esg-acc-wrap .esg-acc__count{display:block;font-family:'Inter',system-ui,sans-serif;font-size:11px;font-weight:400;line-height:1.4;color:#6B7390;margin-top:3px;text-transform:none}\n  .esg-acc-wrap .esg-acc__chev{flex:0 0 auto;width:20px;height:20px;position:relative}\n  .esg-acc-wrap .esg-acc__chev::before,.esg-acc-wrap .esg-acc__chev::after{content:\"\";position:absolute;top:9px;width:11px;height:2px;background:#0A1A3A;transition:transform .2s ease}\n  .esg-acc-wrap .esg-acc__chev::before{left:1px;transform:rotate(45deg)}\n  .esg-acc-wrap .esg-acc__chev::after{right:1px;transform:rotate(-45deg)}\n  .esg-acc-wrap .esg-acc[open] .esg-acc__chev::before{transform:rotate(-45deg)}\n  .esg-acc-wrap .esg-acc[open] .esg-acc__chev::after{transform:rotate(45deg)}\n  .esg-acc-wrap .esg-acc__body{border-top:1px solid #E6E9F0}\n  .esg-acc-wrap .esg-acc__grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:0}\n  .esg-acc-wrap .esg-acc-card{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:12px;padding:12px 16px;text-decoration:none;color:inherit;cursor:pointer;border-bottom:1px solid #E6E9F0;transition:background .15s ease}\n  .esg-acc-wrap .esg-acc-card:last-child{border-bottom:0}\n  .esg-acc-wrap .esg-acc-card:hover,.esg-acc-wrap .esg-acc-card:focus,.esg-acc-wrap .esg-acc-card:focus-within{background:#F8F8F8;text-decoration:none}\n  .esg-acc-wrap .esg-acc-card__thumb{flex:0 0 58px;width:58px;height:58px;background:#fff;border:1px solid #E6E9F0}\n  .esg-acc-wrap .esg-acc-card__thumb img{display:block;width:100%;height:100%;max-width:100%;object-fit:contain;padding:5px;margin:0}\n  .esg-acc-wrap .esg-acc-card__info{flex:1 1 auto;min-width:0}\n  .esg-acc-wrap .esg-acc-card__title{display:block;font-family:'Barlow Condensed','Arial Narrow',sans-serif;font-size:15px;font-weight:700;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:.02em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#0A1A3A;text-decoration:none;margin:0 0 3px}\n  .esg-acc-wrap .esg-acc-card__title:hover,.esg-acc-wrap .esg-acc-card__title:focus-visible{text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:2px}\n  .esg-acc-wrap .esg-acc-card__meta{display:-webkit-box;-webkit-line-clamp:2;-webkit-box-orient:vertical;overflow:hidden;font-family:'Inter',system-ui,sans-serif;font-size:11px;font-weight:400;line-height:1.35;color:#6B7390;margin:0 0 5px}\n  .esg-acc-wrap .esg-acc-card__price{display:flex;align-items:baseline;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:6px}\n  .esg-acc-wrap .esg-acc-card__now{font-family:'Barlow Condensed','Arial Narrow',sans-serif;font-size:17px;font-weight:800;line-height:1;color:#0A1A3A}\n  .esg-acc-wrap .esg-acc-card__was{font-family:'Inter',system-ui,sans-serif;font-size:11px;color:#6B7390;text-decoration:line-through}\n  .esg-acc-wrap .esg-acc-card__save{font-family:'Barlow Condensed','Arial Narrow',sans-serif;font-size:10px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#0A1A3A;border:1px solid #0A1A3A;padding:1px 5px}\n  .esg-acc-wrap .esg-acc-card__out{font-family:'Barlow Condensed','Arial Narrow',sans-serif;font-size:10px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6B7390;border:1px solid #C9CEDB;padding:1px 5px}\n  .esg-acc-wrap .esg-acc-card__unit{font-family:'Inter',system-ui,sans-serif;font-size:11px;color:#6B7390}\n  .esg-acc-wrap .esg-acc-card__add{flex:0 0 auto;display:inline-flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;min-width:56px;padding:7px 13px 6px;background:#fff;border:1px solid #0A1A3A;border-radius:0;color:#0A1A3A;font-family:'Barlow Condensed','Arial Narrow',sans-serif;font-size:14px;font-weight:700;line-height:1;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;white-space:nowrap;cursor:pointer;transition:background .15s ease,color .15s ease}\n  .esg-acc-wrap .esg-acc-card__add:hover,.esg-acc-wrap .esg-acc-card__add:focus-visible{background:#0A1A3A;color:#fff}\n  .esg-acc-wrap .esg-acc-card__add[aria-disabled=\"true\"]{opacity:.45;cursor:default}\n  .esg-acc-wrap .esg-acc-more{grid-column:1 / -1;border-top:1px solid #E6E9F0}\n  .esg-acc-wrap .esg-acc-more__sum{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;gap:7px;padding:11px 16px;cursor:pointer;list-style:none;background:#fff;transition:background .15s ease}\n  .esg-acc-wrap .esg-acc-more__sum::-webkit-details-marker{display:none}\n  .esg-acc-wrap .esg-acc-more__sum::marker{content:\"\"}\n  .esg-acc-wrap .esg-acc-more__sum:hover{background:#F8F8F8}\n  .esg-acc-wrap .esg-acc-more__txt{font-family:'Barlow Condensed','Arial Narrow',sans-serif;font-size:13px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#0A1A3A;line-height:1}\n  .esg-acc-wrap .esg-acc-more__txt--open{display:none}\n  .esg-acc-wrap .esg-acc-more[open] .esg-acc-more__txt--closed{display:none}\n  .esg-acc-wrap .esg-acc-more[open] .esg-acc-more__txt--open{display:inline}\n  .esg-acc-wrap .esg-acc-more__chev{flex:0 0 auto;width:9px;height:9px;border-right:2px solid #0A1A3A;border-bottom:2px solid #0A1A3A;transform:rotate(45deg);margin-top:-3px;transition:transform .2s ease}\n  .esg-acc-wrap .esg-acc-more[open] .esg-acc-more__chev{transform:rotate(-135deg);margin-top:2px}\n  .esg-acc-wrap .esg-acc-more__body{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr;border-top:1px solid #E6E9F0}\n  .esg-acc-wrap .esg-acc-more__body .esg-acc-card:last-child{border-bottom:0}\n  @container (min-width: 860px){\n    .esg-acc-wrap .esg-acc__grid{grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr)}\n    .esg-acc-wrap .esg-acc-more__body{grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr)}\n    .esg-acc-wrap .esg-acc-more__body .esg-acc-card{border-bottom:0;border-right:1px solid #E6E9F0}\n    .esg-acc-wrap .esg-acc-more__body .esg-acc-card:last-child{border-right:0}\n    .esg-acc-wrap .esg-acc-card{border-bottom:0;border-right:1px solid #E6E9F0}\n    .esg-acc-wrap .esg-acc-card:last-child{border-right:0}\n    .esg-acc-wrap .esg-acc__sum{padding:15px 18px}\n  }\n</style>\n\n<div class=\"esg-acc-wrap\" id=\"{{ uid }}\">\n  <details class=\"esg-acc\"{% if is_open %} open{% endif %}>\n    <summary class=\"esg-acc__sum\">\n      <span class=\"esg-acc__sum-txt\">\n        <span class=\"esg-acc__label\">{{ heading_text | escape }}</span>\n        {%- liquid\n          assign plural = 's'\n          if row_count == 1\n            assign plural = ''\n          endif\n          assign sub_final = sub_text | replace: '[count]', row_count | replace: '[s]', plural | replace: '[label]', esg_label | strip\n        -%}\n        {%- if sub_final != blank -%}\n          <span class=\"esg-acc__count\">{{ sub_final | escape }}</span>\n        {%- endif -%}\n      </span>\n      <span class=\"esg-acc__chev\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span>\n    </summary>\n    <div class=\"esg-acc__body\">\n      <div class=\"esg-acc__grid\">{{ rows }}</div>\n    </div>\n  </details>\n</div>\n\n{%- comment -%}\n  ------------------------------------------------------------\n  QUICK VIEW POPUP — self-contained.\n\n  This deliberately does NOT use Alchemy's <quick-add-drawer>.\n  That component copies the fetched page's <product-form> markup,\n  calls form.init(), then Shopify.PaymentButton.init(). Any throw\n  in that chain aborts the rest of the render, and this store is\n  already logging shop-js module load failures. The drawer also\n  only exists when settings.enable_quick_add is on.\n\n  Instead: read the product JSON at /products/<handle>.js, build\n  the popup markup here, and post straight to /cart/add.js. No\n  theme JS, no theme setting, no custom elements.\n  ------------------------------------------------------------\n{%- endcomment -%}\n<style>\n  .esg-qv{position:fixed;inset:0;z-index:2147483000;display:none;align-items:center;justify-content:center;padding:20px;box-sizing:border-box;font-family:'Inter',system-ui,-apple-system,sans-serif}\n  .esg-qv.is-open{display:flex}\n  .esg-qv *,.esg-qv *::before,.esg-qv *::after{box-sizing:border-box}\n  .esg-qv__veil{position:absolute;inset:0;background:rgba(10,26,58,.62)}\n  .esg-qv__box{position:relative;width:100%;max-width:560px;max-height:calc(100vh - 40px);overflow-y:auto;background:#fff;border:1px solid #E6E9F0;border-top:3px solid #0A1A3A;padding:26px 28px 28px}\n  .esg-qv__x{position:absolute;top:10px;right:10px;width:32px;height:32px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;padding:0 0 3px;background:#fff;border:1px solid #E6E9F0;color:#0A1A3A;font-size:22px;line-height:1;cursor:pointer;transition:background .15s ease,color .15s ease}\n  .esg-qv__x:hover,.esg-qv__x:focus-visible{background:#0A1A3A;border-color:#0A1A3A;color:#fff}\n  .esg-qv__head{display:flex;gap:18px;align-items:flex-start;padding-right:30px}\n  .esg-qv__img{flex:0 0 96px;width:96px;height:96px;border:1px solid #E6E9F0;background:#fff;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;overflow:hidden}\n  .esg-qv__img img{max-width:100%;max-height:100%;object-fit:contain;padding:5px;display:block}\n  .esg-qv__ttl{display:block;font-family:'Barlow Condensed','Arial Narrow',sans-serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:800;line-height:1.15;letter-spacing:.01em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#0A1A3A;text-decoration:none;margin:0 0 7px}\n  .esg-qv__ttl:hover,.esg-qv__ttl:focus-visible{text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:2px}\n  .esg-qv__price{display:flex;align-items:baseline;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px}\n  .esg-qv__now{font-family:'Barlow Condensed','Arial Narrow',sans-serif;font-size:24px;font-weight:800;line-height:1;color:#0A1A3A}\n  .esg-qv__was{font-size:12px;color:#6B7390;text-decoration:line-through}\n  .esg-qv__save{font-family:'Barlow Condensed','Arial Narrow',sans-serif;font-size:11px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#0A1A3A;border:1px solid #0A1A3A;padding:2px 6px}\n  .esg-qv__desc{font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;color:#2a3756;margin:18px 0 0}\n  .esg-qv__lbl{display:block;font-family:'Barlow Condensed','Arial Narrow',sans-serif;font-size:12px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6B7390;margin:20px 0 6px}\n  .esg-qv__sel{width:100%;padding:11px 12px;background:#fff;border:1px solid #C9CEDB;border-radius:0;color:#0A1A3A;font-family:'Inter',system-ui,sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:1.3}\n  .esg-qv__sel:focus{outline:2px solid #0A1A3A;outline-offset:1px}\n  .esg-qv__add{width:100%;margin:20px 0 0;padding:15px 18px;background:#0A1A3A;border:1px solid #0A1A3A;border-radius:0;color:#fff;font-family:'Barlow Condensed','Arial Narrow',sans-serif;font-size:17px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase;line-height:1;cursor:pointer;transition:background .15s ease,color .15s ease}\n  .esg-qv__add:hover:not([disabled]),.esg-qv__add:focus-visible:not([disabled]){background:#fff;color:#0A1A3A}\n  .esg-qv__add[disabled]{opacity:.5;cursor:default}\n  .esg-qv__note{font-size:12px;line-height:1.5;color:#2a3756;border-left:3px solid #0A1A3A;background:#F8F8F8;padding:10px 12px;margin:14px 0 0}\n  .esg-qv__full{display:inline-block;font-family:'Barlow Condensed','Arial Narrow',sans-serif;font-size:13px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#0A1A3A;text-decoration:none;border-bottom:1px solid #0A1A3A;margin:18px 0 0}\n  .esg-qv__load{font-size:13px;color:#6B7390;padding:26px 0}\n  .esg-qv__hide{display:none}\n  @media (max-width:560px){\n    .esg-qv{padding:12px}\n    .esg-qv__box{padding:22px 18px 24px}\n    .esg-qv__head{gap:14px}\n    .esg-qv__img{flex:0 0 74px;width:74px;height:74px}\n    .esg-qv__ttl{font-size:19px}\n  }\n</style>\n\n<script>\n  /* Opens for any click on .esg-qv-open or on a card body. The title\n     link is left alone so it still navigates to the full product page. */\n  (function () {\n    if (window.esgQuickView) return;\n    window.esgQuickView = true;\n\n    var root = null, box = null, lastFocus = null, current = null;\n\n    function money(cents) {\n      var s = (Math.round(cents) / 100).toFixed(2).split('.');\n      return '$' + s[0].replace(/\\B(?=(\\d{3})+(?!\\d))/g, ',') + '.' + s[1];\n    }\n\n    /* /products/<handle>.js returns options as objects ({name, position,\n       values}), not strings, so joining them raw prints [object Object].\n       Both shapes are handled since older endpoints return plain strings.\n       Shopify's placeholder name \"Title\" is not shown to shoppers. */\n    function optionLabel(data) {\n      var names = (data.options || []).map(function (o) {\n        return (o && typeof o === 'object') ? (o.name || '') : String(o || '');\n      }).filter(function (n) {\n        return n && n.toLowerCase() !== 'title';\n      });\n      return names.length ? names.join(' / ') : 'Option';\n    }\n\n    function el(tag, cls, txt) {\n      var n = document.createElement(tag);\n      if (cls) n.className = cls;\n      if (txt != null) n.textContent = txt;\n      return n;\n    }\n\n    function build() {\n      root = el('div', 'esg-qv');\n      root.setAttribute('role', 'dialog');\n      root.setAttribute('aria-modal', 'true');\n      root.setAttribute('aria-label', 'Product quick view');\n\n      var veil = el('div', 'esg-qv__veil');\n      veil.addEventListener('click', close);\n\n      box = el('div', 'esg-qv__box');\n\n      var x = el('button', 'esg-qv__x', '\\u00D7');\n      x.type = 'button';\n      x.setAttribute('aria-label', 'Close quick view');\n      x.addEventListener('click', close);\n\n      box.appendChild(x);\n      root.appendChild(veil);\n      root.appendChild(box);\n      document.body.appendChild(root);\n\n      document.addEventListener('keydown', function (e) {\n        if (e.key === 'Escape' && root.classList.contains('is-open')) close();\n      });\n    }\n\n    function close() {\n      if (!root) return;\n      root.classList.remove('is-open');\n      document.documentElement.style.overflow = '';\n      if (lastFocus && lastFocus.focus) lastFocus.focus();\n    }\n\n    function clear() {\n      while (box.childNodes.length > 1) box.removeChild(box.lastChild);\n    }\n\n    function open(card) {\n      if (!root) build();\n      lastFocus = document.activeElement;\n      current = card;\n      clear();\n      box.appendChild(el('p', 'esg-qv__load', 'Loading\\u2026'));\n      root.classList.add('is-open');\n      document.documentElement.style.overflow = 'hidden';\n      box.querySelector('.esg-qv__x').focus();\n\n      var handle = card.getAttribute('data-esg-handle');\n      var url = card.getAttribute('data-product-url') || ('/products/' + handle);\n\n      fetch('/products/' + handle + '.js', { headers: { 'Accept': 'application/json' } })\n        .then(function (r) {\n          if (!r.ok) throw new Error(r.status);\n          return r.json();\n        })\n        .then(function (data) { render(data, card, url); })\n        .catch(function () {\n          clear();\n          box.appendChild(el('p', 'esg-qv__note',\n            'This item could not be loaded here. Open the full product page to continue.'));\n          var a = el('a', 'esg-qv__full', 'View full details');\n          a.href = url;\n          box.appendChild(a);\n        });\n    }\n\n    function render(data, card, url) {\n      clear();\n\n      var head = el('div', 'esg-qv__head');\n      var imgWrap = el('span', 'esg-qv__img');\n      if (data.featured_image) {\n        var img = document.createElement('img');\n        img.src = data.featured_image.replace(/(\\.[a-z]+)(\\?|$)/i, '_240x$1$2');\n        img.alt = data.title;\n        imgWrap.appendChild(img);\n      }\n      head.appendChild(imgWrap);\n\n      var info = el('div');\n      var ttl = el('a', 'esg-qv__ttl', data.title);\n      ttl.href = url;\n      info.appendChild(ttl);\n\n      var priceRow = el('div', 'esg-qv__price');\n      info.appendChild(priceRow);\n      head.appendChild(info);\n      box.appendChild(head);\n\n      var desc = card.getAttribute('data-esg-desc');\n      if (desc) box.appendChild(el('p', 'esg-qv__desc', desc));\n\n      /* Variant picker built from the product JSON rather than copied\n         page markup, so it never depends on theme custom elements. */\n      var sel = null;\n      var live = data.variants.filter(function (v) { return v.available; });\n\n      if (data.variants.length > 1) {\n        box.appendChild(el('span', 'esg-qv__lbl', optionLabel(data)));\n        sel = el('select', 'esg-qv__sel');\n        sel.setAttribute('aria-label', optionLabel(data));\n        data.variants.forEach(function (v) {\n          var o = document.createElement('option');\n          o.value = v.id;\n          o.textContent = v.title + ' \\u2014 ' + money(v.price) + (v.available ? '' : ' \\u2014 Sold out');\n          o.disabled = !v.available;\n          sel.appendChild(o);\n        });\n        if (live.length) sel.value = live[0].id;\n        box.appendChild(sel);\n      }\n\n      var btn = el('button', 'esg-qv__add', 'Add to cart');\n      btn.type = 'button';\n      box.appendChild(btn);\n\n      var note = el('p', 'esg-qv__note esg-qv__hide');\n      box.appendChild(note);\n\n      var full = el('a', 'esg-qv__full', 'View full details');\n      full.href = url;\n      box.appendChild(full);\n\n      function currentVariant() {\n        var id = sel ? parseInt(sel.value, 10) : (live.length ? live[0].id : data.variants[0].id);\n        for (var i = 0; i < data.variants.length; i++) {\n          if (data.variants[i].id === id) return data.variants[i];\n        }\n        return null;\n      }\n\n      function paint() {\n        var v = currentVariant();\n        priceRow.textContent = '';\n        if (!v) return;\n        priceRow.appendChild(el('span', 'esg-qv__now', money(v.price)));\n        if (v.compare_at_price && v.compare_at_price > v.price) {\n          priceRow.appendChild(el('span', 'esg-qv__was', money(v.compare_at_price)));\n          priceRow.appendChild(el('span', 'esg-qv__save',\n            'Save ' + money(v.compare_at_price - v.price).replace(/\\.00$/, '')));\n        }\n        if (v.available) {\n          btn.textContent = 'Add to cart';\n          btn.removeAttribute('disabled');\n        } else {\n          btn.textContent = 'Sold out';\n          btn.setAttribute('disabled', 'disabled');\n        }\n      }\n\n      if (sel) sel.addEventListener('change', paint);\n      paint();\n\n      btn.addEventListener('click', function () {\n        var v = currentVariant();\n        if (!v || !v.available) return;\n        btn.setAttribute('disabled', 'disabled');\n        btn.textContent = 'Adding\\u2026';\n        note.className = 'esg-qv__note esg-qv__hide';\n\n        fetch('/cart/add.js', {\n          method: 'POST',\n          headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json', 'Accept': 'application/json' },\n          body: JSON.stringify({ items: [{ id: v.id, quantity: 1 }] })\n        })\n          .then(function (r) {\n            return r.json().then(function (j) { return { ok: r.ok, body: j }; });\n          })\n          .then(function (res) {\n            if (!res.ok) throw new Error(res.body.description || res.body.message || 'Not added');\n            btn.textContent = 'Added to cart';\n            note.className = 'esg-qv__note';\n            note.textContent = data.title + ' was added to the cart.';\n            refreshCart();\n            setTimeout(paint, 2500);\n          })\n          .catch(function (err) {\n            note.className = 'esg-qv__note';\n            note.textContent = String(err.message || err);\n            paint();\n          });\n      });\n    }\n\n    /* Update the header count and let the theme's cart drawer resync. */\n    function refreshCart() {\n      fetch('/cart.js', { headers: { 'Accept': 'application/json' } })\n        .then(function (r) { return r.json(); })\n        .then(function (cart) {\n          document.querySelectorAll('#CartCount, .js-cart-count').forEach(function (n) {\n            n.textContent = cart.item_count;\n          });\n          document.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent('dispatch:cart-drawer:refresh'));\n        })\n        .catch(function () {});\n    }\n\n    document.addEventListener('click', function (evt) {\n      if (!evt.target.closest) return;\n\n      var trigger = evt.target.closest('.esg-qv-open');\n      var card = trigger ? trigger.closest('.esg-acc-card') : null;\n\n      if (!trigger) {\n        card = evt.target.closest('.esg-acc-card');\n        if (!card) return;\n        /* let real links and buttons behave normally */\n        if (evt.target.closest('a, button')) return;\n      }\n      if (!card) return;\n      if (!card.getAttribute('data-esg-handle')) return;\n\n      evt.preventDefault();\n      open(card);\n    });\n  })();\n</script>\n\n{%- endif -%}"
          }
        },
        "selleasy_lb_upsell_widget_bac_EUgLTt": {
          "type": "shopify://apps/selleasy/blocks/lb-upsell-widget-bac/790c1a03-a71f-4bc1-9869-00dad526d3c2",
          "settings": {}
